window.ETEXTBOOK={"units": [{"id": "u1", "title": "导入问题", "sections": [{"id": "u1_s0", "title": "导入问题", "paras": [{"id": "u1_s0_p1", "buf": ["1 Which styles or schools of Chinese kung fu do you know, and what do you find most impressive about them?"], "text": "1 Which styles or schools of Chinese kung fu do you know, and what do you find most impressive about them?", "chunks": ["1 Which styles or schools of Chinese kung fu do you know, and what do you find most impressive about them?"]}, {"id": "u1_s0_p2", "buf": ["2 Have you ever practised tai chi chuan? How do you think it reflects traditional Chinese culture and philosophy?"], "text": "2 Have you ever practised tai chi chuan? How do you think it reflects traditional Chinese culture and philosophy?", "chunks": ["2 Have you ever practised tai chi chuan? How do you think it reflects traditional Chinese culture and philosophy?"]}, {"id": "u1_s0_p3", "buf": ["3 What are the most popular sports in China?"], "text": "3 What are the most popular sports in China?", "chunks": ["3 What are the most popular sports in China?"]}]}]}, {"id": "u2", "title": "传统体育文化", "sections": [{"id": "u2_s1", "title": "古代体育", "paras": [{"id": "u2_s1_p1", "buf": ["During the Qin and Han dynasties and the Three Kingdoms period, sports began to flourish as an important part of culture in China. Sporting scenes have been recorded over many dynasties in murals (壁画), stone paintings, brick paintings, poems, and other forms of art."], "text": "During the Qin and Han dynasties and the Three Kingdoms period, sports began to flourish as an important part of culture in China. Sporting scenes have been recorded over many dynasties in murals (壁画), stone paintings, brick paintings, poems, and other forms of art.", "chunks": ["During the Qin and Han dynasties and the Three Kingdoms period, sports began to flourish as an important part of culture in China. Sporting scenes have been recorded over many dynasties in murals (壁画), stone paintings, brick paintings, poems, and other forms of art."]}, {"id": "u2_s1_p2", "buf": ["During the Tang Dynasty, jiju (击鞠), an ancient Chinese sport similar to modern-day polo, flourished. People from all walks of life, including the emperor, nobles, and ordinary citizens, loved playing it. Court women were also enthusiastic participants. A group of five painted pottery figurines depicting female polo players were unearthed in Xi'an, Shaanxi Province."], "text": "During the Tang Dynasty, jiju (击鞠), an ancient Chinese sport similar to modern-day polo, flourished. People from all walks of life, including the emperor, nobles, and ordinary citizens, loved playing it. Court women were also enthusiastic participants. A group of five painted pottery figurines depicting female polo players were unearthed in Xi'an, Shaanxi Province.", "chunks": ["During the Tang Dynasty, jiju (击鞠), an ancient Chinese sport similar to modern-day polo, flourished. People from all walks of life, including the emperor, nobles, and ordinary citizens, loved playing it. Court women were also enthusiastic participants. A group of five painted pottery figurines depicting female polo players were unearthed in Xi'an, Shaanxi Province."]}, {"id": "u2_s1_p3", "buf": ["In the Song Dynasty, cuju (蹴鞠), an ancient Chinese game played with an air-filled leather ball similar to modern-day football, became popular. A bronze mirror decorated with a cuju scene, now housed in the Hunan Museum, offers vivid evidence of cuju's popularity during the Southern Song Dynasty. The reverse bears a relief (浮雕) showing young men and women playing the ancient game."], "text": "In the Song Dynasty, cuju (蹴鞠), an ancient Chinese game played with an air-filled leather ball similar to modern-day football, became popular. A bronze mirror decorated with a cuju scene, now housed in the Hunan Museum, offers vivid evidence of cuju's popularity during the Southern Song Dynasty. The reverse bears a relief (浮雕) showing young men and women playing the ancient game.", "chunks": ["In the Song Dynasty, cuju (蹴鞠), an ancient Chinese game played with an air-filled leather ball similar to modern-day football, became popular. A bronze mirror decorated with a cuju scene, now housed in the Hunan Museum, offers vivid evidence of cuju's popularity during the Southern Song Dynasty. The reverse bears a relief (浮雕) showing young men and women playing the ancient game."]}, {"id": "u2_s1_p4", "buf": ["During the Yuan Dynasty, people enjoyed playing a game called chuiwan (捶丸), an ancient Chinese sport similar to golf. As depicted in the mural Chuiwan Tu (《捶丸图》) from the Yuan Dynasty, players used wooden clubs with curved heads to strike balls into a series of holes. Just like golf today, the winner was the one who completed the game with the fewest strokes."], "text": "During the Yuan Dynasty, people enjoyed playing a game called chuiwan (捶丸), an ancient Chinese sport similar to golf. As depicted in the mural Chuiwan Tu (《捶丸图》) from the Yuan Dynasty, players used wooden clubs with curved heads to strike balls into a series of holes. Just like golf today, the winner was the one who completed the game with the fewest strokes.", "chunks": ["During the Yuan Dynasty, people enjoyed playing a game called chuiwan (捶丸), an ancient Chinese sport similar to golf. As depicted in the mural Chuiwan Tu (《捶丸图》) from the Yuan Dynasty, players used wooden clubs with curved heads to strike balls into a series of holes. Just like golf today, the winner was the one who completed the game with the fewest strokes."]}, {"id": "u2_s1_p5", "buf": ["Besides the ball games mentioned above, wrestling, dancing, chess playing, horse racing, and other sports were also popular forms of recreation among ancient Chinese people."], "text": "Besides the ball games mentioned above, wrestling, dancing, chess playing, horse racing, and other sports were also popular forms of recreation among ancient Chinese people.", "chunks": ["Besides the ball games mentioned above, wrestling, dancing, chess playing, horse racing, and other sports were also popular forms of recreation among ancient Chinese people."]}]}, {"id": "u2_s2", "title": "少数民族传统体育", "paras": [{"id": "u2_s2_p1", "buf": ["Ethnic minorities in China engage in traditional sports that reflect their lifestyles and cultural identity."], "text": "Ethnic minorities in China engage in traditional sports that reflect their lifestyles and cultural identity.", "chunks": ["Ethnic minorities in China engage in traditional sports that reflect their lifestyles and cultural identity."]}, {"id": "u2_s2_p2", "buf": ["Since the founding of the People's Republic of China, the Chinese government has been actively promoting the development of ethnic minorities' traditional sports. These sports encompass a wide variety of both competitive and recreational activities. Some well-known examples include the wrestling, horse racing, and archery (射箭) of the Mongolian ethnic group, the yak racing (赛牦牛) of the Tibetan ethnic group, the xiuqiu throwing (抛绣球) of the Zhuang ethnic group, the Korean ethnic group's swing, the Manchu ethnic group's ice-skating, the firework-snatching of the Dong ethnic group, and the top-spinning (打陀螺) games of the Yao ethnic group."], "text": "Since the founding of the People's Republic of China, the Chinese government has been actively promoting the development of ethnic minorities' traditional sports. These sports encompass a wide variety of both competitive and recreational activities. Some well-known examples include the wrestling, horse racing, and archery (射箭) of the Mongolian ethnic group, the yak racing (赛牦牛) of the Tibetan ethnic group, the xiuqiu throwing (抛绣球) of the Zhuang ethnic group, the Korean ethnic group's swing, the Manchu ethnic group's ice-skating, the firework-snatching of the Dong ethnic group, and the top-spinning (打陀螺) games of the Yao ethnic group.", "chunks": ["Since the founding of the People's Republic of China, the Chinese government has been actively promoting the development of ethnic minorities' traditional sports. These sports encompass a wide variety of both competitive and recreational activities. Some well-known examples include the wrestling, horse racing, and archery (射箭) of the Mongolian ethnic group, the yak racing (赛牦牛) of the Tibetan ethnic group, the xiuqiu throwing (抛绣球) of the Zhuang ethnic group, the Korean ethnic group's swing, the Manchu ethnic group's ice-skating, the firework-snatching of the Dong ethnic group, and the top-spinning (打陀螺) games of the Yao ethnic group."]}, {"id": "u2_s2_p3", "buf": ["firework-snatching: a traditional sporting event usually held during the Huapao Festival on the third day of the third lunar month. In the competition, a huapao (a small iron ring wrapped in colourful silk cloth) is fired into the air from a cannon, and team members race to snatch and carry it through opponents' defences to a designated spot. 抢花炮，一般在农历三月初三花炮节举行。\"花炮\"为一铁制圆环，外缠彩色绸布。比赛时，各队选手突破对方的防守将花炮送至指定区域，即为获胜。"], "text": "firework-snatching: a traditional sporting event usually held during the Huapao Festival on the third day of the third lunar month. In the competition, a huapao (a small iron ring wrapped in colourful silk cloth) is fired into the air from a cannon, and team members race to snatch and carry it through opponents' defences to a designated spot. 抢花炮，一般在农历三月初三花炮节举行。\"花炮\"为一铁制圆环，外缠彩色绸布。比赛时，各队选手突破对方的防守将花炮送至指定区域，即为获胜。", "chunks": ["firework-snatching: a traditional sporting event usually held during the Huapao Festival on the third day of the third lunar month. In the competition, a huapao (a small iron ring wrapped in colourful silk cloth) is fired into the air from a cannon, and team members race to snatch and carry it through opponents' defences to a designated spot. 抢花炮，一般在农历三月初三花炮节举行。\"花炮\"为一铁制圆环，外缠彩色绸布。比赛时，各队选手突破对方的防守将花炮送至指定区域，即为获胜。"]}, {"id": "u2_s2_p4", "buf": ["Dragon boat racing, kite flying, shuttlecock kicking (踢毽子), tug-of-war (拔河), yangge, weiqi, qigong, and tai chi chuan are also traditional sports and recreational activities widely enjoyed by people of various ethnic groups throughout China."], "text": "Dragon boat racing, kite flying, shuttlecock kicking (踢毽子), tug-of-war (拔河), yangge, weiqi, qigong, and tai chi chuan are also traditional sports and recreational activities widely enjoyed by people of various ethnic groups throughout China.", "chunks": ["Dragon boat racing, kite flying, shuttlecock kicking (踢毽子), tug-of-war (拔河), yangge, weiqi, qigong, and tai chi chuan are also traditional sports and recreational activities widely enjoyed by people of various ethnic groups throughout China."]}]}, {"id": "u2_s3", "title": "传统体育活动", "paras": [{"id": "u2_s3_p1", "buf": ["Among traditional Chinese physical activities, martial arts are arguably the most representative and typical. Martial arts can also be referred to as kung fu. In terms of character formation, the Chinese character 武 (wu) is made up of 止 (stop) and 戈 (dagger-axe or weapon). The combination of the two components conveys the meaning of \"stopping martial actions\". The character 术 (shu) refers to \"method\", \"art\", or \"skill\". Thus, the term 武术 expresses the Chinese wisdom and cultural values that martial arts exist to prevent conflict rather than cause it. Another interpretation of the term relates to its practical aspect: martial activities practised by individuals or groups, with or without weapons."], "text": "Among traditional Chinese physical activities, martial arts are arguably the most representative and typical. Martial arts can also be referred to as kung fu. In terms of character formation, the Chinese character 武 (wu) is made up of 止 (stop) and 戈 (dagger-axe or weapon). The combination of the two components conveys the meaning of \"stopping martial actions\". The character 术 (shu) refers to \"method\", \"art\", or \"skill\". Thus, the term 武术 expresses the Chinese wisdom and cultural values that martial arts exist to prevent conflict rather than cause it. Another interpretation of the term relates to its practical aspect: martial activities practised by individuals or groups, with or without weapons.", "chunks": ["Among traditional Chinese physical activities, martial arts are arguably the most representative and typical. Martial arts can also be referred to as kung fu. In terms of character formation, the Chinese character 武 (wu) is made up of 止 (stop) and 戈 (dagger-axe or weapon). The combination of the two components conveys the meaning of \"stopping martial actions\". The character 术 (shu) refers to \"method\", \"art\", or \"skill\". Thus, the term 武术 expresses the Chinese wisdom and cultural values that martial arts exist to prevent conflict rather than cause it. Another interpretation of the term relates to its practical aspect: martial activities practised by individuals or groups, with or without weapons."]}, {"id": "u2_s3_p2", "buf": ["Chinese martial arts can be traced back to prehistoric times when ancient people used stones and wooden clubs (棍棒) for hunting, subsistence and self-defence. Over time, these early combative skills evolved into developed martial practices that include kicking, hitting, wrestling, seizing, tumbling, striking, and chopping, whether barehanded or with weapons. Developed and refined over many years, martial arts have become a precious item of national cultural heritage."], "text": "Chinese martial arts can be traced back to prehistoric times when ancient people used stones and wooden clubs (棍棒) for hunting, subsistence and self-defence. Over time, these early combative skills evolved into developed martial practices that include kicking, hitting, wrestling, seizing, tumbling, striking, and chopping, whether barehanded or with weapons. Developed and refined over many years, martial arts have become a precious item of national cultural heritage.", "chunks": ["Chinese martial arts can be traced back to prehistoric times when ancient people used stones and wooden clubs (棍棒) for hunting, subsistence and self-defence. Over time, these early combative skills evolved into developed martial practices that include kicking, hitting, wrestling, seizing, tumbling, striking, and chopping, whether barehanded or with weapons. Developed and refined over many years, martial arts have become a precious item of national cultural heritage."]}, {"id": "u2_s3_p3", "buf": ["With vigorous and graceful movements, martial arts offer practitioners both elegance and strength. People are drawn to martial arts for many reasons: to improve their health and fitness, to hone (磨炼) their defensive skills, to strengthen their mental discipline, and to participate in martial arts competitions or performances."], "text": "With vigorous and graceful movements, martial arts offer practitioners both elegance and strength. People are drawn to martial arts for many reasons: to improve their health and fitness, to hone (磨炼) their defensive skills, to strengthen their mental discipline, and to participate in martial arts competitions or performances.", "chunks": ["With vigorous and graceful movements, martial arts offer practitioners both elegance and strength. People are drawn to martial arts for many reasons: to improve their health and fitness, to hone (磨炼) their defensive skills, to strengthen their mental discipline, and to participate in martial arts competitions or performances."]}]}, {"id": "u2_s4", "title": "中国武术的分类", "paras": [{"id": "u2_s4_p1", "buf": ["Modern Chinese martial arts can be classified into five main categories, as shown in the table below."], "text": "Modern Chinese martial arts can be classified into five main categories, as shown in the table below.", "chunks": ["Modern Chinese martial arts can be classified into five main categories, as shown in the table below."]}, {"id": "u2_s4_p2", "buf": ["traditional Chinese boxing (拳术)：tai chi chuan, southern boxing (南拳), form-mind boxing (形意拳), drunken boxing (醉拳), snake boxing (蛇拳)"], "text": "traditional Chinese boxing (拳术)：tai chi chuan, southern boxing (南拳), form-mind boxing (形意拳), drunken boxing (醉拳), snake boxing (蛇拳)", "chunks": ["traditional Chinese boxing (拳术)：tai chi chuan, southern boxing (南拳), form-mind boxing (形意拳), drunken boxing (醉拳), snake boxing (蛇拳)"]}, {"id": "u2_s4_p3", "buf": ["practice with weapons (器械练习)：• short weapons (e.g., sword, knife)；• long weapons (e.g., spear, staff)；• double weapons (e.g., double sword, double spears)；• flexible weapons (e.g., whip, rope dart)"], "text": "practice with weapons (器械练习)：• short weapons (e.g., sword, knife)；• long weapons (e.g., spear, staff)；• double weapons (e.g., double sword, double spears)；• flexible weapons (e.g., whip, rope dart)", "chunks": ["practice with weapons (器械练习)：• short weapons (e.g., sword, knife)；• long weapons (e.g., spear, staff)；• double weapons (e.g., double sword, double spears)；• flexible weapons (e.g., whip, rope dart)"]}, {"id": "u2_s4_p4", "buf": ["paired practice (对练)：barehanded practice, such as push hands (推手), and weapons practice, such as sword-against-sword and spear-against-spear forms"], "text": "paired practice (对练)：barehanded practice, such as push hands (推手), and weapons practice, such as sword-against-sword and spear-against-spear forms", "chunks": ["paired practice (对练)：barehanded practice, such as push hands (推手), and weapons practice, such as sword-against-sword and spear-against-spear forms"]}, {"id": "u2_s4_p5", "buf": ["group drills (集体演练)：group drills involving more than six people, either barehanded or with weapons, such as group tai chi chuan drills and group staff drills"], "text": "group drills (集体演练)：group drills involving more than six people, either barehanded or with weapons, such as group tai chi chuan drills and group staff drills", "chunks": ["group drills (集体演练)：group drills involving more than six people, either barehanded or with weapons, such as group tai chi chuan drills and group staff drills"]}, {"id": "u2_s4_p6", "buf": ["combat techniques (攻防技术)：combat according to specific rules, such as short-weapon fight"], "text": "combat techniques (攻防技术)：combat according to specific rules, such as short-weapon fight", "chunks": ["combat techniques (攻防技术)：combat according to specific rules, such as short-weapon fight"]}, {"id": "u2_s4_p7", "buf": ["In Chinese martial arts, training is traditionally divided into external work and internal work, two complementary paths that cultivate physical strength and internal energy as a unified discipline."], "text": "In Chinese martial arts, training is traditionally divided into external work and internal work, two complementary paths that cultivate physical strength and internal energy as a unified discipline.", "chunks": ["In Chinese martial arts, training is traditionally divided into external work and internal work, two complementary paths that cultivate physical strength and internal energy as a unified discipline."]}, {"id": "u2_s4_p8", "buf": ["External work, often called \"martial hardness (武术硬功)\", concentrates on conditioning the body through systematic exercises that toughen the muscles, bones, and joints, enhancing resistance to impact, pressure, and falls, and developing explosive strength, stamina, and resilience. Internal work, regarded as the foundation of all martial practice, focuses on directing the mind and breath to generate power from within. Through calm concentration, measured breathing, and controlled movement, practitioners learn to coordinate body and mind."], "text": "External work, often called \"martial hardness (武术硬功)\", concentrates on conditioning the body through systematic exercises that toughen the muscles, bones, and joints, enhancing resistance to impact, pressure, and falls, and developing explosive strength, stamina, and resilience. Internal work, regarded as the foundation of all martial practice, focuses on directing the mind and breath to generate power from within. Through calm concentration, measured breathing, and controlled movement, practitioners learn to coordinate body and mind.", "chunks": ["External work, often called \"martial hardness (武术硬功)\", concentrates on conditioning the body through systematic exercises that toughen the muscles, bones, and joints, enhancing resistance to impact, pressure, and falls, and developing explosive strength, stamina, and resilience. Internal work, regarded as the foundation of all martial practice, focuses on directing the mind and breath to generate power from within. Through calm concentration, measured breathing, and controlled movement, practitioners learn to coordinate body and mind."]}, {"id": "u2_s4_p9", "buf": ["While external work strengthens the body's structure and fighting capacity, internal training refines control, awareness, and the harmonious expression of energy. Together they exemplify the holistic philosophy of Chinese martial arts that true martial mastery lies not in brute strength alone but in the seamless harmony between physical endurance and cultivated inner energy—a balance that embodies the essence of Chinese martial arts culture."], "text": "While external work strengthens the body's structure and fighting capacity, internal training refines control, awareness, and the harmonious expression of energy. Together they exemplify the holistic philosophy of Chinese martial arts that true martial mastery lies not in brute strength alone but in the seamless harmony between physical endurance and cultivated inner energy—a balance that embodies the essence of Chinese martial arts culture.", "chunks": ["While external work strengthens the body's structure and fighting capacity, internal training refines control, awareness, and the harmonious expression of energy. Together they exemplify the holistic philosophy of Chinese martial arts that true martial mastery lies not in brute strength alone but in the seamless harmony between physical endurance and cultivated inner energy—a balance that embodies the essence of Chinese martial arts culture."]}]}, {"id": "u2_s6", "title": "少林拳", "paras": [{"id": "u2_s6_p1", "buf": ["Shaolin Boxing is named after the Shaolin Temple on Mount Song, where the monks have long had a tradition of practising martial skills."], "text": "Shaolin Boxing is named after the Shaolin Temple on Mount Song, where the monks have long had a tradition of practising martial skills.", "chunks": ["Shaolin Boxing is named after the Shaolin Temple on Mount Song, where the monks have long had a tradition of practising martial skills."]}, {"id": "u2_s6_p2", "buf": ["It is said that during the early Tang Dynasty, when Li Shimin (李世民) was besieged (围困) near Luoyang, 13 monks from the Shaolin Temple rescued him. After Li became the emperor of the Tang Dynasty, he rewarded the 13 monks and granted land to the Shaolin Temple. From then on, the Shaolin Temple flourished."], "text": "It is said that during the early Tang Dynasty, when Li Shimin (李世民) was besieged (围困) near Luoyang, 13 monks from the Shaolin Temple rescued him. After Li became the emperor of the Tang Dynasty, he rewarded the 13 monks and granted land to the Shaolin Temple. From then on, the Shaolin Temple flourished.", "chunks": ["It is said that during the early Tang Dynasty, when Li Shimin (李世民) was besieged (围困) near Luoyang, 13 monks from the Shaolin Temple rescued him. After Li became the emperor of the Tang Dynasty, he rewarded the 13 monks and granted land to the Shaolin Temple. From then on, the Shaolin Temple flourished."]}, {"id": "u2_s6_p3", "buf": ["Shaolin Boxing is distinguished by firm, straightforward movements, combining internal stillness with external power and balancing hardness with softness. Its practice emphasises coordinated body mechanics, agile footwork, unity of inner and outer strength, and swift, decisive attacks on an opponent's vital points."], "text": "Shaolin Boxing is distinguished by firm, straightforward movements, combining internal stillness with external power and balancing hardness with softness. Its practice emphasises coordinated body mechanics, agile footwork, unity of inner and outer strength, and swift, decisive attacks on an opponent's vital points.", "chunks": ["Shaolin Boxing is distinguished by firm, straightforward movements, combining internal stillness with external power and balancing hardness with softness. Its practice emphasises coordinated body mechanics, agile footwork, unity of inner and outer strength, and swift, decisive attacks on an opponent's vital points."]}]}, {"id": "u2_s7", "title": "太极拳", "paras": [{"id": "u2_s7_p1", "buf": ["Tai chi chuan is a popular school of Chinese martial arts characterised by slow and gentle movements that are designed for self-defence, physical strengthening, and the promotion of health."], "text": "Tai chi chuan is a popular school of Chinese martial arts characterised by slow and gentle movements that are designed for self-defence, physical strengthening, and the promotion of health.", "chunks": ["Tai chi chuan is a popular school of Chinese martial arts characterised by slow and gentle movements that are designed for self-defence, physical strengthening, and the promotion of health."]}, {"id": "u2_s7_p2", "buf": ["In this art, it is essential that the mind guides the body through graceful, gentle, and firm movements. The origins of tai chi chuan are interpreted in several ways. The most widely accepted view holds that it originated in Chenjiagou in Wenxian County, Henan Province. There are different schools of tai chi chuan, including the Chen (陈), Yang (杨), Wu (吴), Wu (武), Sun (孙), and Zhaobao (赵堡) schools."], "text": "In this art, it is essential that the mind guides the body through graceful, gentle, and firm movements. The origins of tai chi chuan are interpreted in several ways. The most widely accepted view holds that it originated in Chenjiagou in Wenxian County, Henan Province. There are different schools of tai chi chuan, including the Chen (陈), Yang (杨), Wu (吴), Wu (武), Sun (孙), and Zhaobao (赵堡) schools.", "chunks": ["In this art, it is essential that the mind guides the body through graceful, gentle, and firm movements. The origins of tai chi chuan are interpreted in several ways. The most widely accepted view holds that it originated in Chenjiagou in Wenxian County, Henan Province. There are different schools of tai chi chuan, including the Chen (陈), Yang (杨), Wu (吴), Wu (武), Sun (孙), and Zhaobao (赵堡) schools."]}, {"id": "u2_s7_p3", "buf": ["At the opening ceremony of the 2008 Beijing Olympic Games, 2,008 performers dressed in white displayed a breathtaking tai chi chuan demonstration. Moving like a rising tide yet solid as rock, they revealed strength within the graceful, flowing movements, presenting to the world the tai chi ideal of harmony between man and nature. In 2020, tai chi chuan was inscribed on UNESCO's Representative List of the Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity."], "text": "At the opening ceremony of the 2008 Beijing Olympic Games, 2,008 performers dressed in white displayed a breathtaking tai chi chuan demonstration. Moving like a rising tide yet solid as rock, they revealed strength within the graceful, flowing movements, presenting to the world the tai chi ideal of harmony between man and nature. In 2020, tai chi chuan was inscribed on UNESCO's Representative List of the Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity.", "chunks": ["At the opening ceremony of the 2008 Beijing Olympic Games, 2,008 performers dressed in white displayed a breathtaking tai chi chuan demonstration. Moving like a rising tide yet solid as rock, they revealed strength within the graceful, flowing movements, presenting to the world the tai chi ideal of harmony between man and nature. In 2020, tai chi chuan was inscribed on UNESCO's Representative List of the Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity."]}]}, {"id": "u2_s8", "title": "气功", "paras": [{"id": "u2_s8_p1", "buf": ["Qigong is a distinctive Chinese system of breathing, postures, and meditation for self-regulation that promotes health and dates back to ancient times. Practitioners engage in physical and mental exercises to harmonise their mind, breath (vital life energy), and body in order to maintain health and prevent illness."], "text": "Qigong is a distinctive Chinese system of breathing, postures, and meditation for self-regulation that promotes health and dates back to ancient times. Practitioners engage in physical and mental exercises to harmonise their mind, breath (vital life energy), and body in order to maintain health and prevent illness.", "chunks": ["Qigong is a distinctive Chinese system of breathing, postures, and meditation for self-regulation that promotes health and dates back to ancient times. Practitioners engage in physical and mental exercises to harmonise their mind, breath (vital life energy), and body in order to maintain health and prevent illness."]}, {"id": "u2_s8_p2", "buf": ["Qigong is generally divided into two categories. The quiescent (静态的) type requires practitioners to stand, sit, or lie still, concentrate their mind, and breathe in a controlled way to promote circulation and digestion in the body. The mobile (动态的) type involves gentle physical exercises or massage to enhance one's overall health."], "text": "Qigong is generally divided into two categories. The quiescent (静态的) type requires practitioners to stand, sit, or lie still, concentrate their mind, and breathe in a controlled way to promote circulation and digestion in the body. The mobile (动态的) type involves gentle physical exercises or massage to enhance one's overall health.", "chunks": ["Qigong is generally divided into two categories. The quiescent (静态的) type requires practitioners to stand, sit, or lie still, concentrate their mind, and breathe in a controlled way to promote circulation and digestion in the body. The mobile (动态的) type involves gentle physical exercises or massage to enhance one's overall health."]}]}, {"id": "u2_s9", "title": "全民健身", "paras": [{"id": "u2_s9_p1", "buf": ["To promote physical fitness nationwide, China has introduced a range of measures aimed at encouraging more people to make fitness activities an integral part of their daily lives. People throughout the country are paying increasing attention to health and fitness, and their lifestyles have changed a lot. Many public gymnasiums and stadiums across China are widely used, and fitness equipment can be easily found in housing communities and other public spaces. A growing number of people are discovering their own ways to keep fit."], "text": "To promote physical fitness nationwide, China has introduced a range of measures aimed at encouraging more people to make fitness activities an integral part of their daily lives. People throughout the country are paying increasing attention to health and fitness, and their lifestyles have changed a lot. Many public gymnasiums and stadiums across China are widely used, and fitness equipment can be easily found in housing communities and other public spaces. A growing number of people are discovering their own ways to keep fit.", "chunks": ["To promote physical fitness nationwide, China has introduced a range of measures aimed at encouraging more people to make fitness activities an integral part of their daily lives. People throughout the country are paying increasing attention to health and fitness, and their lifestyles have changed a lot. Many public gymnasiums and stadiums across China are widely used, and fitness equipment can be easily found in housing communities and other public spaces. A growing number of people are discovering their own ways to keep fit."]}, {"id": "u2_s9_p2", "buf": ["Kite flying is a traditional Chinese pastime enjoyed by millions across the country. The Weifang International Kite Festival in Shandong Province is a major competition and exhibition that attracts tens of thousands of participants from around the world."], "text": "Kite flying is a traditional Chinese pastime enjoyed by millions across the country. The Weifang International Kite Festival in Shandong Province is a major competition and exhibition that attracts tens of thousands of participants from around the world.", "chunks": ["Kite flying is a traditional Chinese pastime enjoyed by millions across the country. The Weifang International Kite Festival in Shandong Province is a major competition and exhibition that attracts tens of thousands of participants from around the world."]}, {"id": "u2_s9_p3", "buf": ["Horse racing has a long history in China and is a traditional sport enjoyed by many ethnic minorities, such as the Mongol, Tibetan, Uygur, and Kazak peoples. In regions where these groups traditionally live—such as grasslands, high plateaus, and open plains—natural conditions favour horse racing. Over time, the sport has become an integral part of their culture and lifestyle, with regional variations and diverse types of competition."], "text": "Horse racing has a long history in China and is a traditional sport enjoyed by many ethnic minorities, such as the Mongol, Tibetan, Uygur, and Kazak peoples. In regions where these groups traditionally live—such as grasslands, high plateaus, and open plains—natural conditions favour horse racing. Over time, the sport has become an integral part of their culture and lifestyle, with regional variations and diverse types of competition.", "chunks": ["Horse racing has a long history in China and is a traditional sport enjoyed by many ethnic minorities, such as the Mongol, Tibetan, Uygur, and Kazak peoples. In regions where these groups traditionally live—such as grasslands, high plateaus, and open plains—natural conditions favour horse racing. Over time, the sport has become an integral part of their culture and lifestyle, with regional variations and diverse types of competition."]}, {"id": "u2_s9_p4", "buf": ["Yangge is a traditional folk dance accompanied by lively music and singing, in which dancers wear colourful costumes and hold fans, handkerchiefs, or other props. It is very popular in northern China. Its themes are closely connected with people's productive labour and everyday lives."], "text": "Yangge is a traditional folk dance accompanied by lively music and singing, in which dancers wear colourful costumes and hold fans, handkerchiefs, or other props. It is very popular in northern China. Its themes are closely connected with people's productive labour and everyday lives.", "chunks": ["Yangge is a traditional folk dance accompanied by lively music and singing, in which dancers wear colourful costumes and hold fans, handkerchiefs, or other props. It is very popular in northern China. Its themes are closely connected with people's productive labour and everyday lives."]}, {"id": "u2_s9_p5", "buf": ["Tug-of-war in China originated from ancient practices such as towing (拖) boats along riverbanks and military training exercises. In later dynasties, the game evolved from a military exercise into a popular folk sport. In its modern form, two teams of equal size tug on opposite ends of a rope, each trying to pull the central mark on the rope across a designated line to their side. The winning team achieve victory through physical strength and a spirit of cooperation."], "text": "Tug-of-war in China originated from ancient practices such as towing (拖) boats along riverbanks and military training exercises. In later dynasties, the game evolved from a military exercise into a popular folk sport. In its modern form, two teams of equal size tug on opposite ends of a rope, each trying to pull the central mark on the rope across a designated line to their side. The winning team achieve victory through physical strength and a spirit of cooperation.", "chunks": ["Tug-of-war in China originated from ancient practices such as towing (拖) boats along riverbanks and military training exercises. In later dynasties, the game evolved from a military exercise into a popular folk sport. In its modern form, two teams of equal size tug on opposite ends of a rope, each trying to pull the central mark on the rope across a designated line to their side. The winning team achieve victory through physical strength and a spirit of cooperation."]}, {"id": "u2_s9_p6", "buf": ["Rope skipping is an engaging sport for both children and adults. With just a rope, people have invented many ways to play and compete. Skilled participants can spin the rope many times quickly while keeping their feet off the ground during a single jump. With a long rope spun in unison (同时) by two people at opposite ends, even groups of people can play the game. Many schools encourage their students to participate in this healthy activity."], "text": "Rope skipping is an engaging sport for both children and adults. With just a rope, people have invented many ways to play and compete. Skilled participants can spin the rope many times quickly while keeping their feet off the ground during a single jump. With a long rope spun in unison (同时) by two people at opposite ends, even groups of people can play the game. Many schools encourage their students to participate in this healthy activity.", "chunks": ["Rope skipping is an engaging sport for both children and adults. With just a rope, people have invented many ways to play and compete. Skilled participants can spin the rope many times quickly while keeping their feet off the ground during a single jump. With a long rope spun in unison (同时) by two people at opposite ends, even groups of people can play the game. Many schools encourage their students to participate in this healthy activity."]}, {"id": "u2_s9_p7", "buf": ["Shuttlecock kicking is another popular traditional activity. Traditionally, a shuttlecock was made by wrapping a piece of cloth around a coin and inserting a bunch of feathers through the hole in the coin, which helps steady it and control its movement in the air. Nowadays, most shuttlecocks have a rubber or plastic base with feathers fixed in it. There are many styles and techniques of kicking, all aimed at keeping the shuttlecock in the air. Shuttlecock kicking is not only fun but also offers vigorous physical exercise. Nowadays, shuttlecock kicking is enjoying growing popularity among both the young and the old."], "text": "Shuttlecock kicking is another popular traditional activity. Traditionally, a shuttlecock was made by wrapping a piece of cloth around a coin and inserting a bunch of feathers through the hole in the coin, which helps steady it and control its movement in the air. Nowadays, most shuttlecocks have a rubber or plastic base with feathers fixed in it. There are many styles and techniques of kicking, all aimed at keeping the shuttlecock in the air. Shuttlecock kicking is not only fun but also offers vigorous physical exercise. Nowadays, shuttlecock kicking is enjoying growing popularity among both the young and the old.", "chunks": ["Shuttlecock kicking is another popular traditional activity. Traditionally, a shuttlecock was made by wrapping a piece of cloth around a coin and inserting a bunch of feathers through the hole in the coin, which helps steady it and control its movement in the air. Nowadays, most shuttlecocks have a rubber or plastic base with feathers fixed in it. There are many styles and techniques of kicking, all aimed at keeping the shuttlecock in the air. Shuttlecock kicking is not only fun but also offers vigorous physical exercise. Nowadays, shuttlecock kicking is enjoying growing popularity among both the young and the old."]}, {"id": "u2_s9_p8", "buf": ["Nationwide fitness not only reflects China's overall national strength and social progress, but also constitutes an important part of building a well-off society in an all-around way. In 2009, the Chinese government designated 8th August as National Fitness Day. On the one hand, National Fitness Day aims to commemorate the success of the 2008 Beijing Olympic Games. On the other hand, it meets people's growing demand for physical fitness, conveys a healthy sporting spirit, and promotes the concept of healthy living."], "text": "Nationwide fitness not only reflects China's overall national strength and social progress, but also constitutes an important part of building a well-off society in an all-around way. In 2009, the Chinese government designated 8th August as National Fitness Day. On the one hand, National Fitness Day aims to commemorate the success of the 2008 Beijing Olympic Games. On the other hand, it meets people's growing demand for physical fitness, conveys a healthy sporting spirit, and promotes the concept of healthy living.", "chunks": ["Nationwide fitness not only reflects China's overall national strength and social progress, but also constitutes an important part of building a well-off society in an all-around way. In 2009, the Chinese government designated 8th August as National Fitness Day. On the one hand, National Fitness Day aims to commemorate the success of the 2008 Beijing Olympic Games. On the other hand, it meets people's growing demand for physical fitness, conveys a healthy sporting spirit, and promotes the concept of healthy living."]}]}]}, {"id": "u3", "title": "奥运会与中国", "sections": [{"id": "u3_s0", "title": "奥运会与中国", "paras": [{"id": "u3_s0_p1", "buf": ["It was not until 1932, when the 10th Olympic Games were held in Los Angeles, that China was invited to send athletes to compete. The only Chinese participant in the Games was Liu Changchun (刘长春), who entered the 100-metre and 200-metre races. Although he did not achieve notable results, his participation marked the first formal appearance of a Chinese athlete on the Olympic stage."], "text": "It was not until 1932, when the 10th Olympic Games were held in Los Angeles, that China was invited to send athletes to compete. The only Chinese participant in the Games was Liu Changchun (刘长春), who entered the 100-metre and 200-metre races. Although he did not achieve notable results, his participation marked the first formal appearance of a Chinese athlete on the Olympic stage.", "chunks": ["It was not until 1932, when the 10th Olympic Games were held in Los Angeles, that China was invited to send athletes to compete. The only Chinese participant in the Games was Liu Changchun (刘长春), who entered the 100-metre and 200-metre races. Although he did not achieve notable results, his participation marked the first formal appearance of a Chinese athlete on the Olympic stage."]}, {"id": "u3_s0_p2", "buf": ["In 1984, at the Olympic Games in Los Angeles, China, with a team of 225 athletes, won 15 gold medals, 8 silver medals, and 9 bronze medals. Xu Haifeng (许海峰) won the men's 50-metre free pistol event (自选手枪比赛), which was the first gold medal in Chinese Olympic history. This marked the beginning of China's success in the Olympic Games."], "text": "In 1984, at the Olympic Games in Los Angeles, China, with a team of 225 athletes, won 15 gold medals, 8 silver medals, and 9 bronze medals. Xu Haifeng (许海峰) won the men's 50-metre free pistol event (自选手枪比赛), which was the first gold medal in Chinese Olympic history. This marked the beginning of China's success in the Olympic Games.", "chunks": ["In 1984, at the Olympic Games in Los Angeles, China, with a team of 225 athletes, won 15 gold medals, 8 silver medals, and 9 bronze medals. Xu Haifeng (许海峰) won the men's 50-metre free pistol event (自选手枪比赛), which was the first gold medal in Chinese Olympic history. This marked the beginning of China's success in the Olympic Games."]}, {"id": "u3_s0_p3", "buf": ["In 2001, Beijing beat four other cities to win the right to host the 29th Olympic Games in 2008."], "text": "In 2001, Beijing beat four other cities to win the right to host the 29th Olympic Games in 2008.", "chunks": ["In 2001, Beijing beat four other cities to win the right to host the 29th Olympic Games in 2008."]}, {"id": "u3_s0_p4", "buf": ["At the 2008 Beijing Olympic Games, the Chinese delegation, comprised of 639 athletes, participated in 28 sports, 38 disciplines, and 262 events. During the competition, the Chinese athletes displayed impressive athletic skills. China achieved a historic breakthrough with its best-ever Olympic performance, winning a total of 100 medals."], "text": "At the 2008 Beijing Olympic Games, the Chinese delegation, comprised of 639 athletes, participated in 28 sports, 38 disciplines, and 262 events. During the competition, the Chinese athletes displayed impressive athletic skills. China achieved a historic breakthrough with its best-ever Olympic performance, winning a total of 100 medals.", "chunks": ["At the 2008 Beijing Olympic Games, the Chinese delegation, comprised of 639 athletes, participated in 28 sports, 38 disciplines, and 262 events. During the competition, the Chinese athletes displayed impressive athletic skills. China achieved a historic breakthrough with its best-ever Olympic performance, winning a total of 100 medals."]}, {"id": "u3_s0_p5", "buf": ["Building on this success, Beijing made history once again by winning the bid to host the 2022 Winter Olympic Games. This achievement makes Beijing the first city in history to host both the Summer and Winter Olympic Games."], "text": "Building on this success, Beijing made history once again by winning the bid to host the 2022 Winter Olympic Games. This achievement makes Beijing the first city in history to host both the Summer and Winter Olympic Games.", "chunks": ["Building on this success, Beijing made history once again by winning the bid to host the 2022 Winter Olympic Games. This achievement makes Beijing the first city in history to host both the Summer and Winter Olympic Games."]}]}]}, {"id": "u4", "title": "中国优势竞技项目", "sections": [{"id": "u4_s1", "title": "排球", "paras": [{"id": "u4_s1_p1", "buf": ["The Chinese women's volleyball team is renowned for its tenacity, teamwork, pursuit of excellence, and unyielding spirit. Between 1981 and 1986, the team achieved the remarkable \"Five Consecutive Championships\", winning world titles at the World Championships, World Cups, and the 1984 Los Angeles Olympic Games. Since then, it has continued to excel on the world stage, winning additional Olympic gold medals in Athens in 2004 and Rio de Janeiro in 2016, and World Cup titles in 2003, 2015, and 2019. With its 2019 World Cup victory, the team's number of major championship titles across the three most prestigious tournaments—the Olympic Games, World Cup, and World Championship—rose to ten. The Chinese women's volleyball team's perseverance and fighting spirit, first igniting national pride in the 1980s, continues to inspire the Chinese people today."], "text": "The Chinese women's volleyball team is renowned for its tenacity, teamwork, pursuit of excellence, and unyielding spirit. Between 1981 and 1986, the team achieved the remarkable \"Five Consecutive Championships\", winning world titles at the World Championships, World Cups, and the 1984 Los Angeles Olympic Games. Since then, it has continued to excel on the world stage, winning additional Olympic gold medals in Athens in 2004 and Rio de Janeiro in 2016, and World Cup titles in 2003, 2015, and 2019. With its 2019 World Cup victory, the team's number of major championship titles across the three most prestigious tournaments—the Olympic Games, World Cup, and World Championship—rose to ten. The Chinese women's volleyball team's perseverance and fighting spirit, first igniting national pride in the 1980s, continues to inspire the Chinese people today.", "chunks": ["The Chinese women's volleyball team is renowned for its tenacity, teamwork, pursuit of excellence, and unyielding spirit. Between 1981 and 1986, the team achieved the remarkable \"Five Consecutive Championships\", winning world titles at the World Championships, World Cups, and the 1984 Los Angeles Olympic Games. Since then, it has continued to excel on the world stage, winning additional Olympic gold medals in Athens in 2004 and Rio de Janeiro in 2016, and World Cup titles in 2003, 2015, and 2019. With its 2019 World Cup victory, the team's number of major championship titles across the three most prestigious tournaments—the Olympic Games, World Cup, and World Championship—rose to ten. The Chinese women's volleyball team's perseverance and fighting spirit, first igniting national pride in the 1980s, continues to inspire the Chinese people today."]}]}, {"id": "u4_s2", "title": "篮球", "paras": [{"id": "u4_s2_p1", "buf": ["The Chinese Basketball Association (CBA), established in June 1956, is a nationwide, professional, non-profit social organisation voluntarily formed by institutions and individuals dedicated to the development of basketball in China. In 2017, according to the General Administration of Sport of China, the Basketball Administration Center transferred its business responsibilities to the CBA. The launch of the CBA league in 1995 represents a giant step in the development of professional basketball in China."], "text": "The Chinese Basketball Association (CBA), established in June 1956, is a nationwide, professional, non-profit social organisation voluntarily formed by institutions and individuals dedicated to the development of basketball in China. In 2017, according to the General Administration of Sport of China, the Basketball Administration Center transferred its business responsibilities to the CBA. The launch of the CBA league in 1995 represents a giant step in the development of professional basketball in China.", "chunks": ["The Chinese Basketball Association (CBA), established in June 1956, is a nationwide, professional, non-profit social organisation voluntarily formed by institutions and individuals dedicated to the development of basketball in China. In 2017, according to the General Administration of Sport of China, the Basketball Administration Center transferred its business responsibilities to the CBA. The launch of the CBA league in 1995 represents a giant step in the development of professional basketball in China."]}, {"id": "u4_s2_p2", "buf": ["The Chinese women's basketball team is a major force in the world basketball arena. In São Paulo in 1983, they came third in the World Basketball Championships and won bronze at the Los Angeles Olympic Games the following year. In 1992, at the 25th Olympic Games in Barcelona, the team won the silver medal. The Chinese women's team has also performed exceptionally in the Asian Championships (now the FIBA Women's Asia Cup), winning its first title in 1976. This was followed by another in 1986; four consecutive crowns in 1990, 1992, 1994, and 1995; and three straight victories in 2001, 2004, and 2005. China lifted the trophy again in 2009 and 2011 and, after a twelve-year interval, regained the Asian Cup in 2023, bringing its total to twelve Asian titles."], "text": "The Chinese women's basketball team is a major force in the world basketball arena. In São Paulo in 1983, they came third in the World Basketball Championships and won bronze at the Los Angeles Olympic Games the following year. In 1992, at the 25th Olympic Games in Barcelona, the team won the silver medal. The Chinese women's team has also performed exceptionally in the Asian Championships (now the FIBA Women's Asia Cup), winning its first title in 1976. This was followed by another in 1986; four consecutive crowns in 1990, 1992, 1994, and 1995; and three straight victories in 2001, 2004, and 2005. China lifted the trophy again in 2009 and 2011 and, after a twelve-year interval, regained the Asian Cup in 2023, bringing its total to twelve Asian titles.", "chunks": ["The Chinese women's basketball team is a major force in the world basketball arena. In São Paulo in 1983, they came third in the World Basketball Championships and won bronze at the Los Angeles Olympic Games the following year. In 1992, at the 25th Olympic Games in Barcelona, the team won the silver medal. The Chinese women's team has also performed exceptionally in the Asian Championships (now the FIBA Women's Asia Cup), winning its first title in 1976. This was followed by another in 1986; four consecutive crowns in 1990, 1992, 1994, and 1995; and three straight victories in 2001, 2004, and 2005. China lifted the trophy again in 2009 and 2011 and, after a twelve-year interval, regained the Asian Cup in 2023, bringing its total to twelve Asian titles."]}]}, {"id": "u4_s3", "title": "乒乓球", "paras": [{"id": "u4_s3_p1", "buf": ["Table tennis (ping-pong) is very popular throughout China and known as the \"national ball game\" of China. Chinese table tennis players have performed exceptionally well in international competitions. In 1981, all seven championship titles were won by Chinese players at the 36th World Table Tennis Championships—a record in the history of the sport. In 2024, the Chinese women's table tennis team won their 5th consecutive Olympic team title at the Paris Olympics, securing the Chinese delegation's 300th gold medal at the Summer Olympics. By 2025, the Chinese table tennis team have produced a total of 119 world champions."], "text": "Table tennis (ping-pong) is very popular throughout China and known as the \"national ball game\" of China. Chinese table tennis players have performed exceptionally well in international competitions. In 1981, all seven championship titles were won by Chinese players at the 36th World Table Tennis Championships—a record in the history of the sport. In 2024, the Chinese women's table tennis team won their 5th consecutive Olympic team title at the Paris Olympics, securing the Chinese delegation's 300th gold medal at the Summer Olympics. By 2025, the Chinese table tennis team have produced a total of 119 world champions.", "chunks": ["Table tennis (ping-pong) is very popular throughout China and known as the \"national ball game\" of China. Chinese table tennis players have performed exceptionally well in international competitions. In 1981, all seven championship titles were won by Chinese players at the 36th World Table Tennis Championships—a record in the history of the sport. In 2024, the Chinese women's table tennis team won their 5th consecutive Olympic team title at the Paris Olympics, securing the Chinese delegation's 300th gold medal at the Summer Olympics. By 2025, the Chinese table tennis team have produced a total of 119 world champions."]}, {"id": "u4_s3_p2", "buf": ["Table tennis has also made a great contribution to China's diplomacy. In April 1971, after the 31st World Table Tennis Championships in Japan, the Chinese team invited the United States team to visit China. In 1972, the Chinese table tennis team accepted the invitation to pay a return visit to the United States. The friendly exchanges between the table tennis players of the two countries opened the door to warmer relations between China and the United States and became known as \"Ping-Pong Diplomacy\"."], "text": "Table tennis has also made a great contribution to China's diplomacy. In April 1971, after the 31st World Table Tennis Championships in Japan, the Chinese team invited the United States team to visit China. In 1972, the Chinese table tennis team accepted the invitation to pay a return visit to the United States. The friendly exchanges between the table tennis players of the two countries opened the door to warmer relations between China and the United States and became known as \"Ping-Pong Diplomacy\".", "chunks": ["Table tennis has also made a great contribution to China's diplomacy. In April 1971, after the 31st World Table Tennis Championships in Japan, the Chinese team invited the United States team to visit China. In 1972, the Chinese table tennis team accepted the invitation to pay a return visit to the United States. The friendly exchanges between the table tennis players of the two countries opened the door to warmer relations between China and the United States and became known as \"Ping-Pong Diplomacy\"."]}]}, {"id": "u4_s4", "title": "羽毛球", "paras": [{"id": "u4_s4_p1", "buf": ["Since the Sudirman Cup (苏迪曼杯) was first held in 1989, the tournament has taken place 19 times. China claimed the championship for the first time in 1995 and went on to secure its 14th title in 2025. Over the past three decades, the Chinese national team has undoubtedly been the dominant force in this prestigious mixed-team event. By the end of 2024, Chinese badminton players had won the Thomas Cup (汤姆斯杯) 11 times and the Uber Cup (尤伯杯) 16 times."], "text": "Since the Sudirman Cup (苏迪曼杯) was first held in 1989, the tournament has taken place 19 times. China claimed the championship for the first time in 1995 and went on to secure its 14th title in 2025. Over the past three decades, the Chinese national team has undoubtedly been the dominant force in this prestigious mixed-team event. By the end of 2024, Chinese badminton players had won the Thomas Cup (汤姆斯杯) 11 times and the Uber Cup (尤伯杯) 16 times.", "chunks": ["Since the Sudirman Cup (苏迪曼杯) was first held in 1989, the tournament has taken place 19 times. China claimed the championship for the first time in 1995 and went on to secure its 14th title in 2025. Over the past three decades, the Chinese national team has undoubtedly been the dominant force in this prestigious mixed-team event. By the end of 2024, Chinese badminton players had won the Thomas Cup (汤姆斯杯) 11 times and the Uber Cup (尤伯杯) 16 times."]}]}, {"id": "u4_s5", "title": "体操", "paras": [{"id": "u4_s5_p1", "buf": ["For many years, the eyes of the world have been on China during international gymnastics competitions. Chinese gymnasts have proven themselves to be among the most reliable members of the Chinese Olympic squad (代表队) since China began competing at the Games. An American gymnastics expert once remarked that Chinese gymnasts \"make difficult gymnastics look easy\" and \"are talented and hardworking\"."], "text": "For many years, the eyes of the world have been on China during international gymnastics competitions. Chinese gymnasts have proven themselves to be among the most reliable members of the Chinese Olympic squad (代表队) since China began competing at the Games. An American gymnastics expert once remarked that Chinese gymnasts \"make difficult gymnastics look easy\" and \"are talented and hardworking\".", "chunks": ["For many years, the eyes of the world have been on China during international gymnastics competitions. Chinese gymnasts have proven themselves to be among the most reliable members of the Chinese Olympic squad (代表队) since China began competing at the Games. An American gymnastics expert once remarked that Chinese gymnasts \"make difficult gymnastics look easy\" and \"are talented and hardworking\"."]}, {"id": "u4_s5_p2", "buf": ["The Chinese men's team won the team championship title for the first time at the 22nd World Gymnastics Championships in 1983. Since then, Chinese gymnastics has been developing rapidly. At the 2008 Beijing Olympic Games, the Chinese gymnastics team won 9 gold medals—an unprecedented achievement. China excels in a wide range of gymnastics events, such as rings (吊环), parallel bars (双杠), pommel horse (鞍马), and uneven bars (高低杠). Many innovative gymnastics elements originated in China, with several named after the athletes who created them, including the Yuejiu Somersault in the Air (月久空翻), Mo's Somersault in the Air (莫氏空翻), Yang Bo Jump (杨波跳), and Cheng Fei Jump (程菲跳)."], "text": "The Chinese men's team won the team championship title for the first time at the 22nd World Gymnastics Championships in 1983. Since then, Chinese gymnastics has been developing rapidly. At the 2008 Beijing Olympic Games, the Chinese gymnastics team won 9 gold medals—an unprecedented achievement. China excels in a wide range of gymnastics events, such as rings (吊环), parallel bars (双杠), pommel horse (鞍马), and uneven bars (高低杠). Many innovative gymnastics elements originated in China, with several named after the athletes who created them, including the Yuejiu Somersault in the Air (月久空翻), Mo's Somersault in the Air (莫氏空翻), Yang Bo Jump (杨波跳), and Cheng Fei Jump (程菲跳).", "chunks": ["The Chinese men's team won the team championship title for the first time at the 22nd World Gymnastics Championships in 1983. Since then, Chinese gymnastics has been developing rapidly. At the 2008 Beijing Olympic Games, the Chinese gymnastics team won 9 gold medals—an unprecedented achievement. China excels in a wide range of gymnastics events, such as rings (吊环), parallel bars (双杠), pommel horse (鞍马), and uneven bars (高低杠). Many innovative gymnastics elements originated in China, with several named after the athletes who created them, including the Yuejiu Somersault in the Air (月久空翻), Mo's Somersault in the Air (莫氏空翻), Yang Bo Jump (杨波跳), and Cheng Fei Jump (程菲跳)."]}]}, {"id": "u4_s6", "title": "跳水", "paras": [{"id": "u4_s6_p1", "buf": ["China's dominance in diving is undisputed. In their debut at the 2nd Diving World Cup in 1981, Chinese divers won 3 gold medals. More than 40 years later, at the 2025 Diving World Cup Super Final, the Chinese team dominated the competition, sweeping all the titles at the tournament and collecting 9 gold and 4 silver medals for a total of 13. The World Aquatics Championships is another major international tournament in diving. China has long excelled in this event. At the 2025 World Aquatics Championships in Singapore, Chinese divers won 9 gold, 3 silver, and 4 bronze medals, maintaining their dominance on the world stage. Their Olympic record is equally impressive. At the 2008 Beijing Olympic Games, the Chinese \"Dream Team\" of diving earned 7 championship titles out of 8 events. At the 2012 London Olympics, they claimed 6 gold medals. At the 2016 Rio de Janeiro and 2021 Tokyo Olympics, the Chinese diving team won 7 gold medals at each Games. In 2024, they reached an even greater milestone at the Paris Olympics, where they won all 8 gold medals in the diving events—an Olympic history first."], "text": "China's dominance in diving is undisputed. In their debut at the 2nd Diving World Cup in 1981, Chinese divers won 3 gold medals. More than 40 years later, at the 2025 Diving World Cup Super Final, the Chinese team dominated the competition, sweeping all the titles at the tournament and collecting 9 gold and 4 silver medals for a total of 13. The World Aquatics Championships is another major international tournament in diving. China has long excelled in this event. At the 2025 World Aquatics Championships in Singapore, Chinese divers won 9 gold, 3 silver, and 4 bronze medals, maintaining their dominance on the world stage. Their Olympic record is equally impressive. At the 2008 Beijing Olympic Games, the Chinese \"Dream Team\" of diving earned 7 championship titles out of 8 events. At the 2012 London Olympics, they claimed 6 gold medals. At the 2016 Rio de Janeiro and 2021 Tokyo Olympics, the Chinese diving team won 7 gold medals at each Games. In 2024, they reached an even greater milestone at the Paris Olympics, where they won all 8 gold medals in the diving events—an Olympic history first.", "chunks": ["China's dominance in diving is undisputed. In their debut at the 2nd Diving World Cup in 1981, Chinese divers won 3 gold medals. More than 40 years later, at the 2025 Diving World Cup Super Final, the Chinese team dominated the competition, sweeping all the titles at the tournament and collecting 9 gold and 4 silver medals for a total of 13. The World Aquatics Championships is another major international tournament in diving. China has long excelled in this event. At the 2025 World Aquatics Championships in Singapore, Chinese divers won 9 gold, 3 silver, and 4 bronze medals, maintaining their dominance on the world stage. Their Olympic record is equally impressive. At the 2008 Beijing Olympic Games, the Chinese \"Dream Team\" of diving earned 7 championship titles out of 8 events. At the 2012 London Olympics, they claimed 6 gold medals. At the 2016 Rio de Janeiro and 2021 Tokyo Olympics, the Chinese diving team won 7 gold medals at each Games. In 2024, they reached an even greater milestone at the Paris Olympics, where they won all 8 gold medals in the diving events—an Olympic history first."]}]}]}], "vocabA": [{"term": "murals", "zh": "壁画", "q": "During the Qin and Han dynasties and the Three Kingdoms period, sports began to flourish as an important part of culture in China. Sporting scenes have been recorded over many dynasties in murals (壁画)", "tr": "秦汉及三国时期，体育开始兴盛，成为中国文化的重要组成部分。历代以来，体育运动的场景被记录在壁画、石画、砖画、诗歌及其他艺术形式之中。", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "relief", "zh": "浮雕", "q": "In the Song Dynasty, cuju (蹴鞠), an ancient Chinese game played with an air-filled leather ball similar to modern-day football, became popular. A bronze mirror decorated with a cuju scene, now housed i", "tr": "宋朝时，蹴鞠——一种用充气皮球进行、类似现代足球的古代中国游戏——开始流行。一面饰有蹴鞠场景的铜镜（现藏于湖南博物院）为南宋时期蹴鞠的盛行提供了生动佐证，铜镜背面有一幅浮雕，描绘着青年男女玩这一古老游戏的情景。", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "Bronze Mirror with Figures Playing Cuju", "zh": "蹴鞠纹青铜镜", "q": "", "tr": "", "pos": "作品名", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "archery", "zh": "射箭", "q": "Since the founding of the People's Republic of China, the Chinese government has been actively promoting the development of ethnic minorities' traditional sports. These sports encompass a wide variety", "tr": "中华人民共和国成立以来，中国政府积极推动少数民族传统体育的发展。这些体育项目涵盖丰富多样的竞技性和娱乐性活动。其中著名的例子有蒙古族的摔跤、赛马和射箭，藏族的赛牦牛，壮族的抛绣球，朝鲜族的秋千，满族的滑冰，侗族的抢花炮，以及瑶族的打陀螺游戏。", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "yak racing", "zh": "赛牦牛", "q": "Since the founding of the People's Republic of China, the Chinese government has been actively promoting the development of ethnic minorities' traditional sports. These sports encompass a wide variety", "tr": "中华人民共和国成立以来，中国政府积极推动少数民族传统体育的发展。这些体育项目涵盖丰富多样的竞技性和娱乐性活动。其中著名的例子有蒙古族的摔跤、赛马和射箭，藏族的赛牦牛，壮族的抛绣球，朝鲜族的秋千，满族的滑冰，侗族的抢花炮，以及瑶族的打陀螺游戏。", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "xiuqiu throwing", "zh": "抛绣球", "q": "Since the founding of the People's Republic of China, the Chinese government has been actively promoting the development of ethnic minorities' traditional sports. These sports encompass a wide variety", "tr": "中华人民共和国成立以来，中国政府积极推动少数民族传统体育的发展。这些体育项目涵盖丰富多样的竞技性和娱乐性活动。其中著名的例子有蒙古族的摔跤、赛马和射箭，藏族的赛牦牛，壮族的抛绣球，朝鲜族的秋千，满族的滑冰，侗族的抢花炮，以及瑶族的打陀螺游戏。", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "top-spinning", "zh": "打陀螺", "q": "Since the founding of the People's Republic of China, the Chinese government has been actively promoting the development of ethnic minorities' traditional sports. These sports encompass a wide variety", "tr": "中华人民共和国成立以来，中国政府积极推动少数民族传统体育的发展。这些体育项目涵盖丰富多样的竞技性和娱乐性活动。其中著名的例子有蒙古族的摔跤、赛马和射箭，藏族的赛牦牛，壮族的抛绣球，朝鲜族的秋千，满族的滑冰，侗族的抢花炮，以及瑶族的打陀螺游戏。", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "shuttlecock kicking", "zh": "踢毽子", "q": "Dragon boat racing, kite flying, shuttlecock kicking (踢毽子), tug-of-war (拔河), yangge, weiqi, qigong, and tai chi chuan are also traditional sports and recreational activities widely enjoyed by people o", "tr": "赛龙舟、放风筝、踢毽子、拔河、秧歌、围棋、气功和太极拳，也是中国各民族人民广泛喜爱的传统体育与娱乐活动。", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "tug-of-war", "zh": "拔河", "q": "Dragon boat racing, kite flying, shuttlecock kicking (踢毽子), tug-of-war (拔河), yangge, weiqi, qigong, and tai chi chuan are also traditional sports and recreational activities widely enjoyed by people o", "tr": "赛龙舟、放风筝、踢毽子、拔河、秧歌、围棋、气功和太极拳，也是中国各民族人民广泛喜爱的传统体育与娱乐活动。", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "wooden clubs", "zh": "棍棒", "q": "During the Yuan Dynasty, people enjoyed playing a game called chuiwan (捶丸), an ancient Chinese sport similar to golf. As depicted in the mural Chuiwan Tu (《捶丸图》) from the Yuan Dynasty, players used wo", "tr": "元朝时，人们喜爱一种名为捶丸的游戏——一种类似高尔夫的古代中国运动。正如元朝壁画《捶丸图》所描绘的那样，参与者用头部弯曲的木杆击球入一系列球穴。与今天的高尔夫一样，以最少杆数完成比赛者为胜。", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "traditional Chinese boxing", "zh": "拳术", "q": "traditional Chinese boxing (拳术)：tai chi chuan, southern boxing (南拳), form-mind boxing (形意拳), drunken boxing (醉拳), snake boxing (蛇拳)", "tr": "拳术：太极拳、南拳、形意拳、醉拳、蛇拳", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "southern boxing", "zh": "南拳", "q": "traditional Chinese boxing (拳术)：tai chi chuan, southern boxing (南拳), form-mind boxing (形意拳), drunken boxing (醉拳), snake boxing (蛇拳)", "tr": "拳术：太极拳、南拳、形意拳、醉拳、蛇拳", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "form-mind boxing", "zh": "形意拳", "q": "traditional Chinese boxing (拳术)：tai chi chuan, southern boxing (南拳), form-mind boxing (形意拳), drunken boxing (醉拳), snake boxing (蛇拳)", "tr": "拳术：太极拳、南拳、形意拳、醉拳、蛇拳", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "drunken boxing", "zh": "醉拳", "q": "traditional Chinese boxing (拳术)：tai chi chuan, southern boxing (南拳), form-mind boxing (形意拳), drunken boxing (醉拳), snake boxing (蛇拳)", "tr": "拳术：太极拳、南拳、形意拳、醉拳、蛇拳", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "snake boxing", "zh": "蛇拳", "q": "traditional Chinese boxing (拳术)：tai chi chuan, southern boxing (南拳), form-mind boxing (形意拳), drunken boxing (醉拳), snake boxing (蛇拳)", "tr": "拳术：太极拳、南拳、形意拳、醉拳、蛇拳", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "practice with weapons", "zh": "器械练习", "q": "practice with weapons (器械练习)：• short weapons (e.g., sword, knife)；• long weapons (e.g., spear, staff)；• double weapons (e.g., double sword, double spears)；• flexible weapons (e.g., whip, rope dart)", "tr": "器械练习：• 短器械（如剑、刀）；• 长器械（如枪、棍）；• 双器械（如双剑、双枪）；• 软器械（如鞭、绳镖）", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "paired practice", "zh": "对练", "q": "paired practice (对练)：barehanded practice, such as push hands (推手), and weapons practice, such as sword-against-sword and spear-against-spear forms", "tr": "对练：徒手对练，如推手，以及器械对练，如对剑、对枪套路", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "push hands", "zh": "推手", "q": "paired practice (对练)：barehanded practice, such as push hands (推手), and weapons practice, such as sword-against-sword and spear-against-spear forms", "tr": "对练：徒手对练，如推手，以及器械对练，如对剑、对枪套路", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "group drills", "zh": "集体演练", "q": "group drills (集体演练)：group drills involving more than six people, either barehanded or with weapons, such as group tai chi chuan drills and group staff drills", "tr": "集体演练：六人以上参与的集体演练，徒手或持械均可，如集体太极拳演练、集体棍术演练", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "combat techniques", "zh": "攻防技术", "q": "combat techniques (攻防技术)：combat according to specific rules, such as short-weapon fight", "tr": "攻防技术：按特定规则进行的实战，如短器械对抗", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "martial hardness", "zh": "武术硬功", "q": "External work, often called \"martial hardness (武术硬功)\", concentrates on conditioning the body through systematic exercises that toughen the muscles, bones, and joints, enhancing resistance to impact, p", "tr": "外功，常被称为“武术硬功”，着力于通过系统训练增强体质，使肌肉、骨骼和关节变得强韧，提高对撞击、压迫和跌摔的承受能力，并培养爆发力、耐力和韧性。内功被视为一切武术训练的基础，注重以意念和气息引导，从体内生发力量。通过静心专注、匀称呼吸和受控动作，习练者学会协调身心。", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "dagger-axe or weapon", "zh": "戈", "q": "Among traditional Chinese physical activities, martial arts are arguably the most representative and typical. Martial arts can also be referred to as kung fu. In terms of character formation, the Chin", "tr": "在中国传统体育活动中，武术可以说是最具代表性和典型性的。武术又称功夫。从字形上看，汉字“武”由“止”和“戈”（兵器）构成，两个部件组合起来表达“停止武力行为”之意。“术”表示“方法”“艺术”或“技艺”。因此，“武术”一词蕴含着中国智慧与文化价值观：武术的存在是为了防止冲突，而不是挑起冲突。该词还有另一种解释，着眼于其实用层面：个人或群体徒手或持械进行的搏击活动。", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "free pistol event", "zh": "自选手枪比赛", "q": "In 1984, at the Olympic Games in Los Angeles, China, with a team of 225 athletes, won 15 gold medals, 8 silver medals, and 9 bronze medals. Xu Haifeng (许海峰) won the men's 50-metre free pistol event (自", "tr": "1984年洛杉矶奥运会上，中国派出由225名运动员组成的代表团，获得15枚金牌、8枚银牌和9枚铜牌。许海峰在男子50米自选手枪比赛中夺冠，这是中国奥运史上的首枚金牌。这标志着中国在奥运会上夺取佳绩的开端。", "pos": "其他", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "rings", "zh": "吊环", "q": "The Chinese men's team won the team championship title for the first time at the 22nd World Gymnastics Championships in 1983. Since then, Chinese gymnastics has been developing rapidly. At the 2008 Be", "tr": "1983年，中国男队在第22届世界体操锦标赛上首次夺得团体冠军。此后，中国体操发展迅速。在2008年北京奥运会上，中国体操队夺得9枚金牌，创下前所未有的佳绩。中国在众多体操项目上表现突出，如吊环、双杠、鞍马和高低杠。许多创新体操动作源于中国，其中一些以创造者的名字命名，包括月久空翻、莫氏空翻、杨波跳和程菲跳。", "pos": "其他", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "parallel bars", "zh": "双杠", "q": "The Chinese men's team won the team championship title for the first time at the 22nd World Gymnastics Championships in 1983. Since then, Chinese gymnastics has been developing rapidly. At the 2008 Be", "tr": "1983年，中国男队在第22届世界体操锦标赛上首次夺得团体冠军。此后，中国体操发展迅速。在2008年北京奥运会上，中国体操队夺得9枚金牌，创下前所未有的佳绩。中国在众多体操项目上表现突出，如吊环、双杠、鞍马和高低杠。许多创新体操动作源于中国，其中一些以创造者的名字命名，包括月久空翻、莫氏空翻、杨波跳和程菲跳。", "pos": "其他", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "pommel horse", "zh": "鞍马", "q": "The Chinese men's team won the team championship title for the first time at the 22nd World Gymnastics Championships in 1983. Since then, Chinese gymnastics has been developing rapidly. At the 2008 Be", "tr": "1983年，中国男队在第22届世界体操锦标赛上首次夺得团体冠军。此后，中国体操发展迅速。在2008年北京奥运会上，中国体操队夺得9枚金牌，创下前所未有的佳绩。中国在众多体操项目上表现突出，如吊环、双杠、鞍马和高低杠。许多创新体操动作源于中国，其中一些以创造者的名字命名，包括月久空翻、莫氏空翻、杨波跳和程菲跳。", "pos": "其他", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "uneven bars", "zh": "高低杠", "q": "The Chinese men's team won the team championship title for the first time at the 22nd World Gymnastics Championships in 1983. Since then, Chinese gymnastics has been developing rapidly. At the 2008 Be", "tr": "1983年，中国男队在第22届世界体操锦标赛上首次夺得团体冠军。此后，中国体操发展迅速。在2008年北京奥运会上，中国体操队夺得9枚金牌，创下前所未有的佳绩。中国在众多体操项目上表现突出，如吊环、双杠、鞍马和高低杠。许多创新体操动作源于中国，其中一些以创造者的名字命名，包括月久空翻、莫氏空翻、杨波跳和程菲跳。", "pos": "其他", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "Yuejiu Somersault in the Air", "zh": "月久空翻", "q": "The Chinese men's team won the team championship title for the first time at the 22nd World Gymnastics Championships in 1983. Since then, Chinese gymnastics has been developing rapidly. At the 2008 Be", "tr": "1983年，中国男队在第22届世界体操锦标赛上首次夺得团体冠军。此后，中国体操发展迅速。在2008年北京奥运会上，中国体操队夺得9枚金牌，创下前所未有的佳绩。中国在众多体操项目上表现突出，如吊环、双杠、鞍马和高低杠。许多创新体操动作源于中国，其中一些以创造者的名字命名，包括月久空翻、莫氏空翻、杨波跳和程菲跳。", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "Mo's Somersault in the Air", "zh": "莫氏空翻", "q": "The Chinese men's team won the team championship title for the first time at the 22nd World Gymnastics Championships in 1983. Since then, Chinese gymnastics has been developing rapidly. At the 2008 Be", "tr": "1983年，中国男队在第22届世界体操锦标赛上首次夺得团体冠军。此后，中国体操发展迅速。在2008年北京奥运会上，中国体操队夺得9枚金牌，创下前所未有的佳绩。中国在众多体操项目上表现突出，如吊环、双杠、鞍马和高低杠。许多创新体操动作源于中国，其中一些以创造者的名字命名，包括月久空翻、莫氏空翻、杨波跳和程菲跳。", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "Yang Bo Jump", "zh": "杨波跳", "q": "The Chinese men's team won the team championship title for the first time at the 22nd World Gymnastics Championships in 1983. Since then, Chinese gymnastics has been developing rapidly. At the 2008 Be", "tr": "1983年，中国男队在第22届世界体操锦标赛上首次夺得团体冠军。此后，中国体操发展迅速。在2008年北京奥运会上，中国体操队夺得9枚金牌，创下前所未有的佳绩。中国在众多体操项目上表现突出，如吊环、双杠、鞍马和高低杠。许多创新体操动作源于中国，其中一些以创造者的名字命名，包括月久空翻、莫氏空翻、杨波跳和程菲跳。", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "Cheng Fei Jump", "zh": "程菲跳", "q": "The Chinese men's team won the team championship title for the first time at the 22nd World Gymnastics Championships in 1983. Since then, Chinese gymnastics has been developing rapidly. At the 2008 Be", "tr": "1983年，中国男队在第22届世界体操锦标赛上首次夺得团体冠军。此后，中国体操发展迅速。在2008年北京奥运会上，中国体操队夺得9枚金牌，创下前所未有的佳绩。中国在众多体操项目上表现突出，如吊环、双杠、鞍马和高低杠。许多创新体操动作源于中国，其中一些以创造者的名字命名，包括月久空翻、莫氏空翻、杨波跳和程菲跳。", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "Chinese Olympic squad", "zh": "代表队", "q": "For many years, the eyes of the world have been on China during international gymnastics competitions. Chinese gymnasts have proven themselves to be among the most reliable members of the Chinese Olym", "tr": "多年来，在国际体操赛场上，世界的目光始终聚焦中国。自中国开始参加奥运会以来，中国体操运动员已证明自己是奥运会中国代表队中最可靠的成员之一。一位美国体操专家曾评价说，中国体操运动员“让高难度的体操动作看起来轻松自如”，并且“既天赋出众又勤奋刻苦”。", "pos": "其他", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "Sudirman Cup", "zh": "苏迪曼杯", "q": "Since the Sudirman Cup (苏迪曼杯) was first held in 1989, the tournament has taken place 19 times. China claimed the championship for the first time in 1995 and went on to secure its 14th title in 2025. O", "tr": "自1989年苏迪曼杯首次举办以来，该赛事已举办19届。中国于1995年首次夺冠，并在2025年第十四次捧杯。过去三十年间，中国国家队无疑是这项享有盛誉的混合团体赛事中的主导力量。截至2024年底，中国羽毛球选手已11次夺得汤姆斯杯、16次夺得尤伯杯。", "pos": "机构", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "Thomas Cup", "zh": "汤姆斯杯", "q": "Since the Sudirman Cup (苏迪曼杯) was first held in 1989, the tournament has taken place 19 times. China claimed the championship for the first time in 1995 and went on to secure its 14th title in 2025. O", "tr": "自1989年苏迪曼杯首次举办以来，该赛事已举办19届。中国于1995年首次夺冠，并在2025年第十四次捧杯。过去三十年间，中国国家队无疑是这项享有盛誉的混合团体赛事中的主导力量。截至2024年底，中国羽毛球选手已11次夺得汤姆斯杯、16次夺得尤伯杯。", "pos": "机构", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "Uber Cup", "zh": "尤伯杯", "q": "Since the Sudirman Cup (苏迪曼杯) was first held in 1989, the tournament has taken place 19 times. China claimed the championship for the first time in 1995 and went on to secure its 14th title in 2025. O", "tr": "自1989年苏迪曼杯首次举办以来，该赛事已举办19届。中国于1995年首次夺冠，并在2025年第十四次捧杯。过去三十年间，中国国家队无疑是这项享有盛誉的混合团体赛事中的主导力量。截至2024年底，中国羽毛球选手已11次夺得汤姆斯杯、16次夺得尤伯杯。", "pos": "机构", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "National Stadium", "zh": "国家体育场", "q": "", "tr": "", "pos": "建筑", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "martial arts", "zh": "武术", "q": "Among traditional Chinese physical activities, martial arts are arguably the most representative and typical. Martial arts can also be referred to as kung fu. In terms of character formation, the Chin", "tr": "在中国传统体育活动中，武术可以说是最具代表性和典型性的。武术又称功夫。从字形上看，汉字“武”由“止”和“戈”（兵器）构成，两个部件组合起来表达“停止武力行为”之意。“术”表示“方法”“艺术”或“技艺”。因此，“武术”一词蕴含着中国智慧与文化价值观：武术的存在是为了防止冲突，而不是挑起冲突。该词还有另一种解释，着眼于其实用层面：个人或群体徒手或持械进行的搏击活动。", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "Shaolin Boxing", "zh": "少林拳", "q": "Shaolin Boxing is named after the Shaolin Temple on Mount Song, where the monks have long had a tradition of practising martial skills.", "tr": "少林拳因嵩山少林寺而得名，寺中僧人素有习武的传统。", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "dragon boat racing", "zh": "龙舟", "q": "Dragon boat racing, kite flying, shuttlecock kicking (踢毽子), tug-of-war (拔河), yangge, weiqi, qigong, and tai chi chuan are also traditional sports and recreational activities widely enjoyed by people o", "tr": "赛龙舟、放风筝、踢毽子、拔河、秧歌、围棋、气功和太极拳，也是中国各民族人民广泛喜爱的传统体育与娱乐活动。", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "kite flying", "zh": "风筝", "q": "Dragon boat racing, kite flying, shuttlecock kicking (踢毽子), tug-of-war (拔河), yangge, weiqi, qigong, and tai chi chuan are also traditional sports and recreational activities widely enjoyed by people o", "tr": "赛龙舟、放风筝、踢毽子、拔河、秧歌、围棋、气功和太极拳，也是中国各民族人民广泛喜爱的传统体育与娱乐活动。", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "rope skipping", "zh": "跳绳", "q": "Rope skipping is an engaging sport for both children and adults. With just a rope, people have invented many ways to play and compete. Skilled participants can spin the rope many times quickly while k", "tr": "跳绳是一项儿童和成人都喜爱的趣味运动。仅凭一根绳子，人们就发明出许多玩法和比赛方式。技术娴熟的人能在一次跳跃中让双脚离地，同时快速摇绳多圈。用一根长绳由两人在两端同时摇动，甚至可以让一群人一起玩。许多学校鼓励学生参与这项有益健康的活动。", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "firework-snatching", "zh": "抢花炮", "q": "Since the founding of the People's Republic of China, the Chinese government has been actively promoting the development of ethnic minorities' traditional sports. These sports encompass a wide variety", "tr": "中华人民共和国成立以来，中国政府积极推动少数民族传统体育的发展。这些体育项目涵盖丰富多样的竞技性和娱乐性活动。其中著名的例子有蒙古族的摔跤、赛马和射箭，藏族的赛牦牛，壮族的抛绣球，朝鲜族的秋千，满族的滑冰，侗族的抢花炮，以及瑶族的打陀螺游戏。", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "Huapao Festival", "zh": "花炮节", "q": "firework-snatching: a traditional sporting event usually held during the Huapao Festival on the third day of the third lunar month. In the competition, a huapao (a small iron ring wrapped in colourful", "tr": "抢花炮，一般在农历三月初三花炮节举行。“花炮”为一铁制圆环，外缠彩色绸布。比赛时，各队选手突破对方的防守将花炮送至指定区域，即为获胜。", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "nationwide fitness", "zh": "全民健身", "q": "Nationwide fitness not only reflects China's overall national strength and social progress, but also constitutes an important part of building a well-off society in an all-around way. In 2009, the Chi", "tr": "全民健身不仅体现了中国的综合国力和社会进步，也是全面建设小康社会的重要组成部分。2009年，中国政府将8月8日定为“全民健身日”。一方面，“全民健身日”旨在纪念2008年北京奥运会的成功举办；另一方面，它顺应了人们日益增长的健身需求，传递健康的体育精神，倡导健康生活的理念。", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "National Fitness Day", "zh": "全民健身日", "q": "Nationwide fitness not only reflects China's overall national strength and social progress, but also constitutes an important part of building a well-off society in an all-around way. In 2009, the Chi", "tr": "全民健身不仅体现了中国的综合国力和社会进步，也是全面建设小康社会的重要组成部分。2009年，中国政府将8月8日定为“全民健身日”。一方面，“全民健身日”旨在纪念2008年北京奥运会的成功举办；另一方面，它顺应了人们日益增长的健身需求，传递健康的体育精神，倡导健康生活的理念。", "pos": "制度", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "Ping-Pong Diplomacy", "zh": "乒乓球外交", "q": "Table tennis has also made a great contribution to China's diplomacy. In April 1971, after the 31st World Table Tennis Championships in Japan, the Chinese team invited the United States team to visit ", "tr": "乒乓球还为中国外交作出了巨大贡献。1971年4月，在日本举行的第31届世界乒乓球锦标赛结束后，中国队邀请美国队访华。1972年，中国乒乓球队应邀回访美国。两国乒乓球运动员之间的友好交流，为中美关系的缓和打开了大门，被称为“乒乓外交”。", "pos": "事件", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "table tennis", "zh": "乒乓球", "q": "Table tennis (ping-pong) is very popular throughout China and known as the \"national ball game\" of China. Chinese table tennis players have performed exceptionally well in international competitions. ", "tr": "乒乓球在中国广受欢迎，被誉为中国的“国球”。中国乒乓球运动员在国际比赛中表现出色。1981年，在第36届世界乒乓球锦标赛上，中国选手包揽了全部七项冠军，创造了这项运动史上的纪录。2024年，中国乒乓球女队在巴黎奥运会上实现奥运女团五连冠，为中国代表团赢得夏季奥运会第300枚金牌。截至2025年，中国乒乓球队共培养出119位世界冠军。", "pos": "其他", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "volleyball", "zh": "排球", "q": "The Chinese women's volleyball team is renowned for its tenacity, teamwork, pursuit of excellence, and unyielding spirit. Between 1981 and 1986, the team achieved the remarkable \"Five Consecutive Cham", "tr": "中国女排以坚韧、协作、追求卓越和顽强拼搏的精神著称。1981年至1986年间，中国女排创造了“五连冠”的辉煌战绩，先后在世锦赛、世界杯和1984年洛杉矶奥运会上夺得世界冠军。此后，她们继续在世界舞台上大放异彩，又夺得2004年雅典奥运会和2016年里约奥运会金牌，并在2003年、2015年和2019年三度问鼎世界杯。凭借2019年世界杯的夺冠，中国女排在奥运会、世界杯和世锦赛这三大顶级赛事中夺得的主要冠军总数上升至十个。中国女排的坚韧与拼搏精神早在20世纪80年代就点燃了民族自豪感，至今仍激励着中国人民。", "pos": "其他", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "basketball", "zh": "篮球", "q": "The Chinese Basketball Association (CBA), established in June 1956, is a nationwide, professional, non-profit social organisation voluntarily formed by institutions and individuals dedicated to the de", "tr": "中国篮球协会（CBA）成立于1956年6月，是由致力于中国篮球事业发展的机构和个人自愿组成的全国性、专业性、非营利性社会组织。2017年，据国家体育总局消息，篮球运动管理中心将其业务职责移交中国篮协。1995年CBA联赛的创办，标志着中国职业篮球发展迈出巨大一步。", "pos": "其他", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "badminton", "zh": "羽毛球", "q": "Since the Sudirman Cup (苏迪曼杯) was first held in 1989, the tournament has taken place 19 times. China claimed the championship for the first time in 1995 and went on to secure its 14th title in 2025. O", "tr": "自1989年苏迪曼杯首次举办以来，该赛事已举办19届。中国于1995年首次夺冠，并在2025年第十四次捧杯。过去三十年间，中国国家队无疑是这项享有盛誉的混合团体赛事中的主导力量。截至2024年底，中国羽毛球选手已11次夺得汤姆斯杯、16次夺得尤伯杯。", "pos": "其他", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "gymnastics", "zh": "体操", "q": "For many years, the eyes of the world have been on China during international gymnastics competitions. Chinese gymnasts have proven themselves to be among the most reliable members of the Chinese Olym", "tr": "多年来，在国际体操赛场上，世界的目光始终聚焦中国。自中国开始参加奥运会以来，中国体操运动员已证明自己是奥运会中国代表队中最可靠的成员之一。一位美国体操专家曾评价说，中国体操运动员“让高难度的体操动作看起来轻松自如”，并且“既天赋出众又勤奋刻苦”。", "pos": "其他", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "diving", "zh": "跳水", "q": "China's dominance in diving is undisputed. In their debut at the 2nd Diving World Cup in 1981, Chinese divers won 3 gold medals. More than 40 years later, at the 2025 Diving World Cup Super Final, the", "tr": "中国在跳水项目上的统治地位毋庸置疑。1981年，中国跳水队首次参加第2届跳水世界杯，便夺得3枚金牌。40多年后，在2025年跳水世界杯超级总决赛上，中国队统治了赛场，包揽赛事全部冠军，共收获9枚金牌和4枚银牌，合计13枚。世界游泳锦标赛是另一项跳水重大国际赛事，中国长期以来在该赛事上表现出色。在2025年新加坡世界游泳锦标赛上，中国跳水选手获得9枚金牌、3枚银牌和4枚铜牌，保持了在世界舞台上的统治地位。他们的奥运战绩同样令人瞩目。在2008年北京奥运会上，中国跳水“梦之队”在8个项目中夺得7项冠军。在2012年伦敦奥运会上，他们夺得6枚金牌。在2016年里约奥运会和2021年东京奥运会上，中国跳水队每届均获7枚金牌。2024年，他们在巴黎奥运会上达到更高的里程碑，包揽跳水项目全部8枚金牌，这在奥运历史上尚属首次。", "pos": "其他", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "Chinese Basketball Association", "zh": "中国篮球协会", "q": "The Chinese Basketball Association (CBA), established in June 1956, is a nationwide, professional, non-profit social organisation voluntarily formed by institutions and individuals dedicated to the de", "tr": "中国篮球协会（CBA）成立于1956年6月，是由致力于中国篮球事业发展的机构和个人自愿组成的全国性、专业性、非营利性社会组织。2017年，据国家体育总局消息，篮球运动管理中心将其业务职责移交中国篮协。1995年CBA联赛的创办，标志着中国职业篮球发展迈出巨大一步。", "pos": "机构", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "General Administration of Sport of China", "zh": "国家体育总局", "q": "The Chinese Basketball Association (CBA), established in June 1956, is a nationwide, professional, non-profit social organisation voluntarily formed by institutions and individuals dedicated to the de", "tr": "中国篮球协会（CBA）成立于1956年6月，是由致力于中国篮球事业发展的机构和个人自愿组成的全国性、专业性、非营利性社会组织。2017年，据国家体育总局消息，篮球运动管理中心将其业务职责移交中国篮协。1995年CBA联赛的创办，标志着中国职业篮球发展迈出巨大一步。", "pos": "机构", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "external work", "zh": "外功", "q": "In Chinese martial arts, training is traditionally divided into external work and internal work, two complementary paths that cultivate physical strength and internal energy as a unified discipline.", "tr": "在中国武术中，训练传统上分为外功和内功，二者互为补充，将身体力量与内在能量作为一门统一的功夫加以培养。", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "internal work", "zh": "内功", "q": "In Chinese martial arts, training is traditionally divided into external work and internal work, two complementary paths that cultivate physical strength and internal energy as a unified discipline.", "tr": "在中国武术中，训练传统上分为外功和内功，二者互为补充，将身体力量与内在能量作为一门统一的功夫加以培养。", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "UNESCO", "zh": "联合国教科文组织", "q": "At the opening ceremony of the 2008 Beijing Olympic Games, 2,008 performers dressed in white displayed a breathtaking tai chi chuan demonstration. Moving like a rising tide yet solid as rock, they rev", "tr": "在2008年北京奥运会开幕式上，2008名身着白衣的表演者献上了一场令人叹为观止的太极拳表演。他们动如潮涌，稳如磐石，在优美流畅的动作中展现出力量，向世界呈现了太极拳天人合一的理念。2020年，太极拳被列入联合国教科文组织人类非物质文化遗产代表作名录。", "pos": "机构", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "Representative List of the Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity", "zh": "人类非物质文化遗产代表作名录", "q": "At the opening ceremony of the 2008 Beijing Olympic Games, 2,008 performers dressed in white displayed a breathtaking tai chi chuan demonstration. Moving like a rising tide yet solid as rock, they rev", "tr": "在2008年北京奥运会开幕式上，2008名身着白衣的表演者献上了一场令人叹为观止的太极拳表演。他们动如潮涌，稳如磐石，在优美流畅的动作中展现出力量，向世界呈现了太极拳天人合一的理念。2020年，太极拳被列入联合国教科文组织人类非物质文化遗产代表作名录。", "pos": "制度", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "Tang Dynasty", "zh": "唐朝", "q": "During the Tang Dynasty, jiju (击鞠), an ancient Chinese sport similar to modern-day polo, flourished. People from all walks of life, including the emperor, nobles, and ordinary citizens, loved playing ", "tr": "唐朝时，击鞠——一种类似现代马球的古代中国运动——十分兴盛。上至皇帝、贵族，下至平民百姓，社会各阶层都喜爱这项运动，宫廷妇女也热衷参与。在陕西省西安出土了一组五件描绘女子打马球的彩绘陶俑。", "pos": "朝代", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "Song Dynasty", "zh": "宋朝", "q": "In the Song Dynasty, cuju (蹴鞠), an ancient Chinese game played with an air-filled leather ball similar to modern-day football, became popular. A bronze mirror decorated with a cuju scene, now housed i", "tr": "宋朝时，蹴鞠——一种用充气皮球进行、类似现代足球的古代中国游戏——开始流行。一面饰有蹴鞠场景的铜镜（现藏于湖南博物院）为南宋时期蹴鞠的盛行提供了生动佐证，铜镜背面有一幅浮雕，描绘着青年男女玩这一古老游戏的情景。", "pos": "朝代", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "Yuan Dynasty", "zh": "元朝", "q": "During the Yuan Dynasty, people enjoyed playing a game called chuiwan (捶丸), an ancient Chinese sport similar to golf. As depicted in the mural Chuiwan Tu (《捶丸图》) from the Yuan Dynasty, players used wo", "tr": "元朝时，人们喜爱一种名为捶丸的游戏——一种类似高尔夫的古代中国运动。正如元朝壁画《捶丸图》所描绘的那样，参与者用头部弯曲的木杆击球入一系列球穴。与今天的高尔夫一样，以最少杆数完成比赛者为胜。", "pos": "朝代", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "Beijing Olympic Games", "zh": "北京奥运会", "q": "At the opening ceremony of the 2008 Beijing Olympic Games, 2,008 performers dressed in white displayed a breathtaking tai chi chuan demonstration. Moving like a rising tide yet solid as rock, they rev", "tr": "在2008年北京奥运会开幕式上，2008名身着白衣的表演者献上了一场令人叹为观止的太极拳表演。他们动如潮涌，稳如磐石，在优美流畅的动作中展现出力量，向世界呈现了太极拳天人合一的理念。2020年，太极拳被列入联合国教科文组织人类非物质文化遗产代表作名录。", "pos": "事件", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "football", "zh": "足球", "q": "In the Song Dynasty, cuju (蹴鞠), an ancient Chinese game played with an air-filled leather ball similar to modern-day football, became popular. A bronze mirror decorated with a cuju scene, now housed i", "tr": "宋朝时，蹴鞠——一种用充气皮球进行、类似现代足球的古代中国游戏——开始流行。一面饰有蹴鞠场景的铜镜（现藏于湖南博物院）为南宋时期蹴鞠的盛行提供了生动佐证，铜镜背面有一幅浮雕，描绘着青年男女玩这一古老游戏的情景。", "pos": "其他", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "polo", "zh": "马球", "q": "During the Tang Dynasty, jiju (击鞠), an ancient Chinese sport similar to modern-day polo, flourished. People from all walks of life, including the emperor, nobles, and ordinary citizens, loved playing ", "tr": "唐朝时，击鞠——一种类似现代马球的古代中国运动——十分兴盛。上至皇帝、贵族，下至平民百姓，社会各阶层都喜爱这项运动，宫廷妇女也热衷参与。在陕西省西安出土了一组五件描绘女子打马球的彩绘陶俑。", "pos": "其他", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "golf", "zh": "高尔夫球", "q": "During the Yuan Dynasty, people enjoyed playing a game called chuiwan (捶丸), an ancient Chinese sport similar to golf. As depicted in the mural Chuiwan Tu (《捶丸图》) from the Yuan Dynasty, players used wo", "tr": "元朝时，人们喜爱一种名为捶丸的游戏——一种类似高尔夫的古代中国运动。正如元朝壁画《捶丸图》所描绘的那样，参与者用头部弯曲的木杆击球入一系列球穴。与今天的高尔夫一样，以最少杆数完成比赛者为胜。", "pos": "其他", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "sword play", "zh": "剑术", "q": "", "tr": "", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "broadsword play", "zh": "刀法", "q": "", "tr": "", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "spear play", "zh": "枪术", "q": "", "tr": "", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}, {"term": "staff play", "zh": "棍法", "q": "", "tr": "", "pos": "术语", "src": "原文"}], "vocabB": [], "examsA": [{"term": "", "zh": "", "cn": "功夫（Kong Fu) 是中国武术（martial arts）的俗称。", "en": "Kung Fu is a common name for Chinese martial arts.", "ptype": "真题", "cat": "真题A", "map": "功夫（Kung Fu）与武术", "set": "CET4 2016·06·S1", "src": "CET4 2016·06·S1", "cls": "Chapter 6", "tip": "断句:单分句;核心=①;话题:补主语(→Kung Fu);文化:功夫→S1 kung fu(库定译，China Daily HK)；中国武术→S1 Chinese martial arts(库；en.chinaculture)｜原卷括注 martial arts；备注:[原卷如此]（\"（Kong Fu) \"为全角左括号＋半角右括号＋空格，照抄不改）", "ta": "补主语（话题→主语，Li & Thompson 1976）；意合→形合。", "te": "词性转换（\"俗称\"→a common name for，名词化）；增补（a）。", "srcEn": "S2 · 整句无官方译文（整理编译）；\"功夫\"见 China Daily HK（库定译 kung fu），S1；\"中国武术\"见 China Daily / en.chinaculture.org（Chinese martial arts），S1。", "rp": "`a common name for`（L2·PC）；`Chinese martial arts`（L2·PC）。"}, {"term": "", "zh": "", "cn": "中国武术的起源可以追溯到自卫的需要，狩猎活动以及古代中国的军士训练。", "en": "The origin of Chinese martial arts can be traced back to the need for self-defense, hunting activities, and the military training of ancient China.", "ptype": "真题", "cat": "真题A", "map": "功夫（Kung Fu）与武术", "set": "CET4 2016·06·S1", "src": "CET4 2016·06·S1", "cls": "Chapter 6", "tip": "断句:单分句;核心=①;②③④→并列宾语;话题:补主语(→The origin of Chinese martial arts);受事→被动(can be traced back to)(CL-04);文化:中国武术→S1 Chinese martial arts；自卫→S1 self-defense(库；en.chinaculture)；狩猎活动→S4 hunting activities(库通译)；军事训练→S1 military training(库；en.chinaculture)", "ta": "补主语（\"中国武术的起源\"→The origin of…）；受事→被动（can be traced back to，CL-04）；修饰语后置（连淑能 1993）。", "te": "词性转换（\"起源\"→origin，名词化）；动词短语\"追溯到\"→be traced back to（Vinay & Darbelnet 1958）；增补（并列宾语 and）。", "srcEn": "S2 · 整句无官方译文（整理编译）；\"中国武术\"见 China Daily / en.chinaculture.org，S1；\"自卫\"（self-defense）、\"军事训练\"（military training）见 en.chinaculture.org，S1；\"狩猎活动\"未定位同形，S4。", "rp": "`be traced back to`（L2·PC）；`the need for`（L2·PC）。"}, {"term": "", "zh": "", "cn": "它是中国传统体育运动的一种，年轻人和老年人都练。", "en": "It is one of the traditional Chinese sports, and it is practiced by both young and old people.", "ptype": "真题", "cat": "真题A", "map": "功夫（Kung Fu）与武术", "set": "CET4 2016·06·S1", "src": "CET4 2016·06·S1", "cls": "Chapter 6", "tip": "断句:分句①/②;核心=①;②→并列独立句/被动;话题:补主语(承前→It)；文化:传统体育运动→S1 traditional and popular national sport(库；en.chinaculture)；老年人→the elderly(通译)", "ta": "补主语；意合→形合（and，连淑能 1993）；受事→被动（is practiced by，CL-04）。", "te": "动词\"练\"→be practiced（受事被动化，Vinay & Darbelnet 1958）；增补（both）。", "srcEn": "S2 · 整句无官方译文（整理编译）；\"传统体育运动\"库内作 traditional and popular national sport（en.chinaculture.org），S1。", "rp": "`one of the …`（L2·PC）；`be practiced by`（L2·PC）。"}, {"term": "", "zh": "", "cn": "它已逐渐演变成了中国文化的独特元素。", "en": "It has gradually evolved into a unique element of Chinese culture.", "ptype": "真题", "cat": "真题A", "map": "功夫（Kung Fu）与武术", "set": "CET4 2016·06·S1", "src": "CET4 2016·06·S1", "cls": "Chapter 6", "tip": "断句:单分句;核心=①;时锚:已→现在完成时;话题:补主语(承前→It)；文化:中国文化→Chinese culture(S1通译)", "ta": "补主语；时态呼应（现在完成时，连淑能 1993）。", "te": "动词\"演变\"→evolve into；词性转换（\"元素\"→element）；增补（gradually）。", "srcEn": "S2 · 整句无官方译文（整理编译）。", "rp": "`evolve into`（L2·PC）；`a unique element of`（L2·PC）。"}, {"term": "", "zh": "", "cn": "作为中国的国宝，武术有上百种不同的风格，是世界上练得最多的武术形式。", "en": "As a national treasure of China, martial arts has hundreds of different styles and is the most widely practiced form of martial arts in the world.", "ptype": "真题", "cat": "真题A", "map": "功夫（Kung Fu）与武术", "set": "CET4 2016·06·S1", "src": "CET4 2016·06·S1", "cls": "Chapter 6", "tip": "断句:分句①②③;核心=②;①→状语(As a national treasure);③→并列/评价;话题:补主语(→martial arts);文化:国宝→S1 a national treasure(库；新华英文/China Daily Asia)；武术→martial arts｜Chinese martial arts", "ta": "补主语；状语前置（As…，连淑能 1993）；意合→形合（and）。", "te": "词性转换（\"练得最多\"→the most widely practiced，比较级名词化）；增补（different）。", "srcEn": "S2 · 整句无官方译文（整理编译）；\"国宝\"见新华英文 / China Daily Asia（a national treasure），S1。", "rp": "`a national treasure`（L2·PC）；`the most widely practiced`（L2·PC）。"}, {"term": "", "zh": "", "cn": "有些风格模仿了动物的动作，还有一些则受到了中国哲学思想，神话和传说的启发。", "en": "Some styles imitate the movements of animals, while others are inspired by Chinese philosophy, myths and legends.", "ptype": "真题", "cat": "真题A", "map": "功夫（Kung Fu）与武术", "set": "CET4 2016·06·S1", "src": "CET4 2016·06·S1", "cls": "Chapter 6", "tip": "断句:分句①/②;核心=并列对照;逻辑:并列对照→while|and;话题:补主语(→Some styles / others);受事→被动(others→are inspired by)(CL-04);文化:哲学思想→S1 philosophy(库；en.chinaculture)；神话和传说→S1 folk tale(库；en.chinaculture)｜myth and legend；备注:[原卷如此]（\"中国哲学思想，神话和传说\"用半角逗号并列，通常应作顿号，照抄不改）", "ta": "补主语；意合→形合（对照 while，连淑能 1993）；受事→被动（are inspired by，CL-04）；对比显性化。", "te": "动词\"模仿\"→imitate；惯用等值（\"受到…启发\"→be inspired by）；增补（the）。", "srcEn": "S2 · 整句无官方译文（整理编译）；\"哲学思想\"库内作 philosophy（en.chinaculture.org），S1；\"传说\"库内作 folk tale（en.chinaculture.org），S1（myth/legend 为并行候选）。", "rp": "`while …`（对照，L2·SB）→ 本句实例：Some styles imitate the movements of animals, while others are inspired by Chinese philosophy, myths and legends；`be inspired by`（L2·PC）。"}, {"term": "", "zh": "", "cn": "太极拳 (Taijiquan)起源于中国古代，是中国武术 (martialart)的一个重要分支。", "en": "Taijiquan originated in ancient China and is an important branch of Chinese martial arts.", "ptype": "真题", "cat": "真题A", "map": "太极拳（Taijiquan）", "set": "CET4 2022·09·S1", "src": "CET4 2022·09·S1", "cls": "Chapter 6", "tip": "断句:分句①/②;核心=①;②→并列(and)/同位;话题:补主语(→Taijiquan)；文化:太极拳→S1 Taijiquan(原卷括注)；中国武术→Chinese martial arts｜原卷括注 martialart；备注:[原卷如此]（\"太极拳 \"为半角空格＋半角括号；\"(martialart)\"疑漏空格/复数，照抄不改）", "ta": "补主语；意合→形合（and，连淑能 1993）。", "te": "动词\"起源于\"→originated in；词性转换（\"分支\"→branch）；增补（important）。", "srcEn": "S2 · 整句无官方译文（整理编译）；\"太极拳\"从原卷括注 Taijiquan（同源优先），S1；\"中国武术\"见 China Daily / en.chinaculture.org，S1。", "rp": "`originate in`（L2·PC）；`an important branch of`（L2·PC）。"}, {"term": "", "zh": "", "cn": "练太极拳最初是为了自卫，现在是促进身心健康的有效锻炼方式。", "en": "Practicing Taijiquan was originally for self-defense, but now it is an effective way of exercise to promote physical and mental health.", "ptype": "真题", "cat": "真题A", "map": "太极拳（Taijiquan）", "set": "CET4 2022·09·S1", "src": "CET4 2022·09·S1", "cls": "Chapter 6", "tip": "断句:分句①/②;核心=①;②→转折(but);逻辑:转折→but;时锚:最初→一般过去；现在→一般现在;话题:动名词主语(→Practicing Taijiquan)(CL-02)；文化:自卫→S1 self-defense；身心健康→S1 physical and mental health(库；China Daily)", "ta": "动名词主语（\"练太极拳\"→Practicing…，连淑能 1993）；意合→形合（but，连淑能 1993）；时态呼应（过去→现在，连淑能 1993）。", "te": "词性转换（\"锻炼方式\"→a way of exercise）；增补（originally/effective）；动词\"促进\"→promote。", "srcEn": "S2 · 整句无官方译文（整理编译）；\"自卫\"见 en.chinaculture.org（self-defense），S1；\"身心健康\"官媒作 physical and mental health（库；China Daily），S1。", "rp": "`a way of`（L2·PC）；`physical and mental health`（L2·PC）。"}, {"term": "", "zh": "", "cn": "大量研究表明，这种锻炼方式有助于保持力量、灵活性和平衡力，并减少压力和焦虑。", "en": "A large number of studies show that this form of exercise helps maintain strength, flexibility and balance, and reduce stress and anxiety.", "ptype": "真题", "cat": "真题A", "map": "太极拳（Taijiquan）", "set": "CET4 2022·09·S1", "src": "CET4 2022·09·S1", "cls": "Chapter 6", "tip": "断句:分句①/②;核心=①;②→宾语从句(that…);话题:补主语(→A large number of studies)；触发[有助于]→help+V|be conducive to+V-ing；文化:力量/灵活性/平衡力→strength/flexibility/balance(S4通译)；压力/焦虑→stress/anxiety(S4通译)", "ta": "补主语；意合→形合（that 宾语从句，连淑能 1993）。", "te": "动词并列（\"保持…减少…\"→maintain… / reduce…）；动词\"表明\"→show；增补（a large number of）。", "srcEn": "S2 · 整句无官方译文（整理编译）。", "rp": "`a large number of`（L2·PC）；`help V`（L2·PC）。"}, {"term": "", "zh": "", "cn": "太极拳练习起来既容易又愉快，通过轻柔、流畅的动作，促使心情平静、头脑清晰。", "en": "Taijiquan is both easy and pleasant to practice, and through gentle, flowing movements it helps calm the mind and clear the head.", "ptype": "真题", "cat": "真题A", "map": "太极拳（Taijiquan）", "set": "CET4 2022·09·S1", "src": "CET4 2022·09·S1", "cls": "Chapter 6", "tip": "断句:分句①/②;核心=①;②→方式状语(through…)/伴随;触发[既…又]→both…and…；话题:补主语(→Taijiquan)；文化:轻柔流畅的动作→gentle, flowing movements(S4通译)", "ta": "补主语；方式状语（through…，连淑能 1993）；触发构式（both…and…，认知构式翻译观）。", "te": "增补（both/and）；动词\"促使\"→help V；词性转换（\"平静/清晰\"→calm/clear）。", "srcEn": "S2 · 整句无官方译文（整理编译）。", "rp": "`both … and …`（L2·SB）→ 本句实例：Taijiquan is both easy and pleasant to practice；`through …`（L2·PC）。"}, {"term": "", "zh": "", "cn": "今天，太极拳已经传播到世界各地，深受广大健身者的喜爱。", "en": "Today, Taijiquan has spread to all parts of the world and is deeply loved by fitness enthusiasts.", "ptype": "真题", "cat": "真题A", "map": "太极拳（Taijiquan）", "set": "CET4 2022·09·S1", "src": "CET4 2022·09·S1", "cls": "Chapter 6", "tip": "断句:分句①/②;核心=①;②→并列/被动(深受喜爱→be loved by)(CL-04);时锚:已经→现在完成时；今天→一般现在;话题:补主语(→Taijiquan)；文化:健身者→fitness enthusiasts(S4通译)", "ta": "补主语；时态呼应（现在完成时，连淑能 1993）；受事→被动（be loved by，CL-04）；意合→形合（and）。", "te": "惯用等值（\"深受…喜爱\"→be deeply loved by）；动词\"传播\"→spread；增补（deeply）。", "srcEn": "S2 · 整句无官方译文（整理编译）。", "rp": "`spread to`（L2·PC）；`be loved by`（L2·PC）。"}], "examsB": [{"term": "", "zh": "", "cn": "自行车曾经是中国城乡最主要的交通工具，中国一度被称为“自行车王国”。", "en": "Bicycles were once the most important means of transportation in China's cities and countryside, and China was once called the \"kingdom of bicycles.\"", "ptype": "真题", "cat": "真题B", "map": "自行车与共享单车", "set": "CET6 2018·06·S3", "src": "CET6 2018·06·S3", "cls": "Chapter 6", "tip": "断句:分句①/②;核心=①;②→并列(and)/被动评价;时锚:曾经/一度→一般过去时;话题:补主语(→Bicycles)；受事→被动(被称为→be called)(CL-04)；文化:自行车王国→S4 the \"kingdom of bicycles\"(官媒偶见，未定位库内定译)", "ta": "补主语；受事→被动（be called，CL-04）；意合→形合（and，连淑能 1993）；时态呼应（一般过去时，连淑能 1993）。", "te": "惯用等值（\"交通工具\"→means of transportation）；名词化（\"王国\"→kingdom）；增补（most/once）。", "srcEn": "S2 · 整句无官方译文（整理编译）；\"自行车王国\"无 whitelist 定译，标 S4（the \"kingdom of bicycles\" / the \"Bicycle Kingdom\" 并存）。", "rp": "`means of transportation`（L2·PC）；`be called`（L2·PC）。"}, {"term": "", "zh": "", "cn": "如今，随着城市交通拥堵和空气污染日益严重，骑自行车又开始起来。", "en": "Nowadays, as urban traffic congestion and air pollution are getting worse, riding bicycles is becoming popular again.", "ptype": "真题", "cat": "真题B", "map": "自行车与共享单车", "set": "CET6 2018·06·S3", "src": "CET6 2018·06·S3", "cls": "Chapter 6", "tip": "断句:分句①/②;核心=②;①→背景/原因状语(As…,主句)|(With…,主句);触发[随着]→As…,主句；时锚:如今→一般现在时;话题:动名词主语(→riding bicycles)(CL-02)；文化:交通拥堵→S1 traffic congestion(库；China Daily)；空气污染→air pollution(S1通译)；备注:[原卷如此]（\"骑自行车又开始起来\"疑漏字/措辞异常，照抄不改）", "ta": "补主语；状语前置（As…, 主句，连淑能 1993）；动名词主语（\"骑自行车\"→riding bicycles，Li & Thompson 1976）。", "te": "惯用等值（\"日益严重\"→getting worse）；增补（again/urban）。", "srcEn": "S2 · 整句无官方译文（整理编译）；\"交通拥堵\"见 China Daily（traffic congestion），S1。", "rp": "`as … 主句`（时间/原因从句，L2·SB）→ 本句实例：… as urban traffic congestion and air pollution are getting worse, riding bicycles is becoming popular again；`traffic congestion`（L2·PC）。"}, {"term": "", "zh": "", "cn": "近来，中国企业家将移动互联网技术与传统自行车结合在一起，发明了一种称为共享单车（shared bikes）的商业模式。", "en": "Recently, Chinese entrepreneurs have combined mobile Internet technology with traditional bicycles to invent a business model called shared bikes.", "ptype": "真题", "cat": "真题B", "map": "自行车与共享单车", "set": "CET6 2018·06·S3", "src": "CET6 2018·06·S3", "cls": "Chapter 6", "tip": "断句:分句①/②;核心=①;②→目的状语(to invent…)|结果;时锚:近来→现在完成时;话题:补主语(→Chinese entrepreneurs)；文化:共享单车→S1 shared bikes(原卷括注＋库；China Daily)；移动互联网→mobile Internet(S4通译)；商业模式→business model(S4通译)", "ta": "补主语；目的状语化（to invent…，连淑能 1993）；时态呼应（现在完成时，连淑能 1993）。", "te": "动词\"结合\"→combine … with …；分词后置（\"称为…的\"→called…）；增补（a）。", "srcEn": "S2 · 整句无官方译文（整理编译）；\"共享单车\"从原卷括注 shared bikes（同源优先），库内亦作 shared bikes（China Daily），S1。", "rp": "`combine A with B`（L2·PC）；`a … called …`（L2·PC）。"}, {"term": "", "zh": "", "cn": "共享单车的出现使骑车出行更加方便，人们仅需一部手机就可以随时使用共享单车。", "en": "The emergence of shared bikes has made cycling much more convenient, and people can use shared bikes at any time with just a smartphone.", "ptype": "真题", "cat": "真题B", "map": "自行车与共享单车", "set": "CET6 2018·06·S3", "src": "CET6 2018·06·S3", "cls": "Chapter 6", "tip": "断句:分句①/②;核心=①;②→并列/说明(and);触发[使]→make+A+adj|enable+A+to+V|allow+A+to+V;话题:补主语(→The emergence of shared bikes)；文化:共享单车→S1 shared bikes；一部手机→just a smartphone(通译)", "ta": "补主语；触发构式（make＋A＋adj，认知构式翻译观）；意合→形合（and，连淑能 1993）。", "te": "词性转换（\"出现\"→The emergence of，名词化）；使役 make；增补（much/just）。", "srcEn": "S2 · 整句无官方译文（整理编译）；\"共享单车\"同源 shared bikes，S1。", "rp": "`make A + adj`（L2·SB）→ 本句实例：The emergence of shared bikes has made cycling much more convenient；`at any time`（L2·PC）。"}, {"term": "", "zh": "", "cn": "为了鼓励人们骑车出行，很多城市修建了自行车道。", "en": "To encourage people to cycle, many cities have built bicycle lanes.", "ptype": "真题", "cat": "真题B", "map": "自行车与共享单车", "set": "CET6 2018·06·S3", "src": "CET6 2018·06·S3", "cls": "Chapter 6", "tip": "断句:分句①/②;核心=②;①→目的状语(To V…)(CL-07);话题:补主语(→many cities)；文化:自行车道→bicycle lanes|cycle lanes(S4通译)；骑车出行→cycle|travel by bike", "ta": "目的状语前置（To V…，连淑能 1993）；补主语；时态呼应（现在完成时）。", "te": "动词\"鼓励\"→encourage；增补（have）。", "srcEn": "S2 · 整句无官方译文（整理编译）。", "rp": "`To V …, 主句`（目的，CL-07）（L2·SB）→ 本句实例：To encourage people to cycle, many cities have built bicycle lanes；`encourage sb to V`（L2·PC）。"}, {"term": "", "zh": "", "cn": "现在，越来越多的中国人也喜欢通过骑车健身。", "en": "Now, more and more Chinese people also like to keep fit by cycling.", "ptype": "真题", "cat": "真题B", "map": "自行车与共享单车", "set": "CET6 2018·06·S3", "src": "CET6 2018·06·S3", "cls": "Chapter 6", "tip": "断句:单分句;核心=①;时锚:现在→一般现在时;话题:补主语(→more and more Chinese people)；文化:健身→keep fit|work out(库「锻炼 exercise」互参)；骑车→cycling", "ta": "补主语；方式状语（by V-ing，连淑能 1993）。", "te": "动词\"健身\"→keep fit；动名词（\"骑车\"→cycling）；增补（also）。", "srcEn": "S2 · 整句无官方译文（整理编译）；\"健身/锻炼\"库内收 exercise / work out（China Daily 行文支撑），S1。", "rp": "`more and more`（L2·PC）；`by V-ing`（L2·SB）。"}, {"term": "", "zh": "", "cn": "近年来，中国政府进一步加大体育馆建设投资，以更好地满足人们快速增长的健身需求。", "en": "In recent years, the Chinese government has further increased investment in the construction of sports venues to better meet people's rapidly growing demand for fitness.", "ptype": "真题", "cat": "真题B", "map": "体育馆建设与全民健身", "set": "CET6 2018·12·S3", "src": "CET6 2018·12·S3", "cls": "Chapter 6", "tip": "断句:分句①/②;核心=①;②→目的状语(to better meet…)(CL-07);时锚:近年来→现在完成时;话题:补主语(→the Chinese government)；文化:体育馆→S1 sports venues(库；China Daily)｜stadiums and gymnasiums；(快速增长的)健身需求→S1 a surging public appetite for sports(库；China Daily)", "ta": "补主语；目的状语化（to better meet…，连淑能 1993）；时态呼应（现在完成时，连淑能 1993）。", "te": "名词化（\"投资\"→investment，\"建设\"→construction）；动词\"加大\"→increase；增补（further）。", "srcEn": "S2 · 整句无官方译文（整理编译）；\"体育馆（体育场馆）\"库内作 sports venues（China Daily），S1；\"（快速增长的）健身需求\"库内作 a surging public appetite for sports（China Daily），S1。", "rp": "`increase investment in`（L2·PC）；`meet the demand for`（L2·PC）。"}, {"term": "", "zh": "", "cn": "除了新建体育馆外，许多城市换采取了改造旧工厂和商业建筑等措施，来增加当地体育馆的数量。", "en": "In addition to building new sports venues, many cities have also taken measures such as repurposing old factories and commercial buildings to increase the number of local sports venues.", "ptype": "真题", "cat": "真题B", "map": "体育馆建设与全民健身", "set": "CET6 2018·12·S3", "src": "CET6 2018·12·S3", "cls": "Chapter 6", "tip": "断句:分句①/②;核心=②;①→补充状语(In addition to V-ing…);②→目的状语(to increase…);话题:补主语(→many cities)；文化:改造旧工厂/商业建筑→repurposing old factories and commercial buildings(库「改造利用闲置空间 repurposing underused spaces」互参)；备注:[原卷如此]（\"换采取了\"疑为\"还采取了\"或\"采取了\"之误，照抄不改）", "ta": "状语前置（In addition to…，连淑能 1993）；补主语；目的状语化（to increase…，连淑能 1993）。", "te": "名词化（\"数量\"→number）；惯用等值（\"采取措施\"→take measures）；增补（also/such as）。", "srcEn": "S2 · 整句无官方译文（整理编译）；\"改造利用闲置空间（旧厂房等）\"库内作 repurposing underused spaces（China Daily），S1。", "rp": "`in addition to V-ing`（L2·PC）；`take measures`（L2·PC）。"}, {"term": "", "zh": "", "cn": "在政府资金的支持下，越来越多的体育馆向公众免费开放，或者只收取少量费用。", "en": "With the support of government funds, more and more sports venues are open to the public free of charge, or charge only a small fee.", "ptype": "真题", "cat": "真题B", "map": "体育馆建设与全民健身", "set": "CET6 2018·12·S3", "src": "CET6 2018·12·S3", "cls": "Chapter 6", "tip": "断句:单分句;核心=①;话题:句首框架状语(在…支持下)前置;补主语(→more and more sports venues)；文化:政府资金→S4 with the support of government funds(库通译)；免费开放→S1 free admission ｜open to the public free of charge(库；People's Daily Online)", "ta": "状语前置（With…，连淑能 1993）；补主语；意合→形合（or）。", "te": "动词转系表（\"开放\"→are open）；增补（only/small）。", "srcEn": "S2 · 整句无官方译文（整理编译）；\"免费开放（向公众）\"库内作 free admission / open to the public free of charge（People's Daily Online），S1；\"政府资金（在…支持下）\"库内作 with the support of government funds，S4。", "rp": "`with the support of`（L2·PC）；`free of charge`（L2·PC）。"}, {"term": "", "zh": "", "cn": "许多体育馆通过应用现代信息技术大大提高了服务质量。", "en": "Many sports venues have greatly improved their service quality through the application of modern information technology.", "ptype": "真题", "cat": "真题B", "map": "体育馆建设与全民健身", "set": "CET6 2018·12·S3", "src": "CET6 2018·12·S3", "cls": "Chapter 6", "tip": "断句:单分句;核心=①;话题:补主语(→many sports venues)；逻辑:方式状语→through V-ing;时锚:提高了→现在完成时;文化:信息技术→S1 information technology(库；China Daily)；服务质量→service quality(S4通译)", "ta": "补主语；方式状语（through…，连淑能 1993）；时态呼应（现在完成时，连淑能 1993）。", "te": "名词化（\"应用\"→application）；动词\"提高\"→improve；增补（greatly）。", "srcEn": "S2 · 整句无官方译文（整理编译）；\"信息技术\"见 China Daily（information technology），S1。", "rp": "`through the application of`（L2·PC）；`improve service quality`（L2·PC）。"}, {"term": "", "zh": "", "cn": "人民可以方便地在线预订场地和付费。", "en": "People can conveniently book venues and pay online.", "ptype": "真题", "cat": "真题B", "map": "体育馆建设与全民健身", "set": "CET6 2018·12·S3", "src": "CET6 2018·12·S3", "cls": "Chapter 6", "tip": "断句:单分句;核心=①;话题:补主语(→people)；文化:在线预订和付费→book and pay online ｜book and pay in advance(S4通译)；备注:[原卷如此]（\"人民\"疑为\"人们\"之误，照抄不改）", "ta": "补主语；副词饰动（\"方便地\"→conveniently，连淑能 1993）。", "te": "副词化（\"方便地\"→conveniently）；动词并列（\"预订…付费\"→book … and pay …）。", "srcEn": "S2 · 整句无官方译文（整理编译）；\"预订和支付（费用）\"库内作 book and pay in advance（S4 通译）。", "rp": "`book and pay online`（L2·PC）。"}, {"term": "", "zh": "", "cn": "可以预见，随着运动设施的不断改善，愈来愈多的人将会去体育馆健身。", "en": "It can be predicted that, as sports facilities continue to improve, more and more people will go to sports venues to keep fit.", "ptype": "真题", "cat": "真题B", "map": "体育馆建设与全民健身", "set": "CET6 2018·12·S3", "src": "CET6 2018·12·S3", "cls": "Chapter 6", "tip": "断句:分句①/②;核心=②;①→评注句(It can be predicted that…);触发[随着]→As…,主句；时锚:将会→将来时;话题:补主语(→more and more people)；文化:运动设施→S1 sports facilities(库；China Daily)；备注:[原卷如此]（\"愈来愈多\"为\"越来越多\"的变体，照抄不改）", "ta": "形式主语（It can be predicted that…，连淑能 1993）；状语从句（as…，连淑能 1993）；时态呼应（将来时，连淑能 1993）。", "te": "惯用等值（\"可以预见\"→It can be predicted that…）；目的状语（to keep fit）；增补（continue to）。", "srcEn": "S2 · 整句无官方译文（整理编译）；\"体育设施（运动设施）\"库内作 sports facilities（China Daily），S1。", "rp": "`It can be predicted that …`（L2·SB）→ 本句实例：It can be predicted that … more and more people will go to sports venues to keep fit；`as … 主句`（L2·SB）。"}], "exercises": [], "vocabHF": []}